(function(){
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(w,origin)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const Q=(id,senseId,errorType,prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain)=>({id,senseId,type:'辨義與用法',errorType,prompt,options:[answer,d1,d2],answer,explain});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistakes,quiz)=>D(w,{etymology:E(w,origin),contexts,mistakes,quiz});
P('wage','From Old North French wage, “pledge or payment,” from a Germanic source; as a verb it later came to mean carry on a war or campaign.',[C('wage.s1','工资','The seasonal workers negotiated a higher wage before the harvest began.','季節性工人在收割開始前協商提高工資。','earn / pay / negotiate a wage','Noun: regular payment for work, often calculated by time or task.','The workers negotiate their pay.'),C('wage.s2','开展；发动','The two groups waged a long campaign to protect the wetland.','兩個團體長期展開保護濕地的運動。','wage a campaign / war / struggle','Verb: carry on or conduct a campaign, war, or struggle.','They actively conduct a campaign.')],[M('The union waged a campaign by refusing to organize, protest, or take any action.','The union abandoned its campaign when it refused to organize or take action.','To wage a campaign is to conduct it, not to do nothing.')],[Q('wage.q1','wage.s1','meaning','What did the seasonal workers negotiate?','The payment they would receive for their work.','A military campaign.','A waiting room reservation.','Wage as a noun means payment for work.'),Q('wage.q2','wage.s2','context','What did the groups do to protect the wetland?','They conducted a sustained campaign.','They paid each other an hourly salary.','They stopped all activity.','Wage as a verb means conduct a campaign or struggle.'),Q('wage.q3','wage.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses wage as a payment?','an hourly wage','wage a campaign','wage a war','An hourly wage is money paid for work.'),Q('wage.q4','wage.s2','grammar','Which phrase commonly follows wage as a verb?','wage a campaign','wage at a salary','wage with a receipt','The verb takes a direct object such as a campaign.')]);
P('wager','From wage + -er, “a pledge or stake”; it names a bet and the act of betting.',[C('wager.s1','赌注','Her wager was ten dollars on the final score being tied at halftime.','她下注十美元，賭上半場結束時比分會打平。','place / win / lose a wager','Noun: money or something else risked on the result of an uncertain event.','She risks money on a predicted result.'),C('wager.s2','打赌','I would wager that the early train will be less crowded than the later one.','我敢打賭，早班火車會比晚一班人少。','wager that…; wager on + outcome','Verb: bet or state a confident prediction about an uncertain outcome.','The speaker makes a prediction as a bet.')],[M('He wagered ten dollars on the race but refused to risk or bet anything.','He predicted the winner but placed no wager on the race.','A wager involves risking a stake; refusing to risk anything is not wagering money.')],[Q('wager.q1','wager.s1','meaning','What did she risk on the halftime score?','Ten dollars.','Her train ticket.','A courtroom decision.','A wager is a stake risked on an uncertain result.'),Q('wager.q2','wager.s2','context','What does “I would wager the train is late” express?','A confident prediction framed as a bet.','A guaranteed fact already checked.','A request for a higher salary.','As a verb, wager can mean bet or make a prediction.'),Q('wager.q3','wager.s1','distinction','Which item is the wager in a card game?','The money placed at risk before the hand.','The final score after the game.','The person serving at the table.','The stake risked is the wager.'),Q('wager.q4','wager.s2','grammar','Which construction is natural?','She wagered that the team would win.','She wagered to the team that it win.','She wagered the team winning on.','Wager can take a that-clause to state a prediction.')]);
P('wages','From wage, from Old North French wage, “payment”; the plural commonly means a person’s regular earnings and can also mean the consequences of an action.',[C('wages.s1','薪水','The factory pays its workers weekly wages and provides paid leave.','工廠每週發薪給員工，並提供有薪假期。','earn / pay / weekly wages','Noun plural: regular money paid to a worker for labor.','The workers receive pay each week.'),C('wages.s2','代价；后果','The novel calls loneliness the wages of his years of selfish choices.','小說把孤獨稱作他多年自私選擇所付出的代價。','the wages of + action / conduct','Noun plural: the results or consequences of an action, often harmful.','The result follows from his choices.')],[M('The wages of her careful planning were a failure caused by an unrelated accident.','The wages of her careless planning were a failure caused by her poor decisions.','Wages in this figurative phrase are consequences that follow from the actions named.')],[Q('wages.q1','wages.s1','meaning','What does the factory pay weekly?','Money earned by workers for their labor.','A bet on a sports match.','A penalty for a crime.','Wages commonly means regular earnings.'),Q('wages.q2','wages.s2','context','What are “the wages of selfish choices” in the novel?','The consequences that follow from those choices.','The worker’s weekly paycheck.','A prize unrelated to behavior.','The figurative phrase means consequences or results.'),Q('wages.q3','wages.s1','distinction','Which use refers to employment pay?','The firm raised the wages of its staff.','The wages of neglect were costly repairs.','He placed wages on a horse race.','The first sentence describes money paid to employees.'),Q('wages.q4','wages.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','The wages of haste were several avoidable errors.','Her wages arrived in her bank account on Friday.','The wager was ten dollars.','The first uses wages to mean consequences.')]);
P('waggle','From wag + the frequentative ending -le, suggesting repeated small movements.',[C('waggle.s1','来回摇动（动词）','The puppy waggled its tail when the children returned from school.','孩子們放學回來時，小狗來回搖著尾巴。','waggle a finger / tail','Verb: move something with repeated short side-to-side or up-and-down motions.','The tail moves repeatedly from side to side.'),C('waggle.s2','摇动（名词）','With one final waggle of the handle, the loose tap began to run.','把手最後晃了幾下，鬆動的水龍頭便開始出水。','give something a waggle','Noun: a short repeated shaking movement.','The handle receives several small shakes.')],[M('The puppy waggled its tail by keeping it perfectly still throughout the greeting.','The puppy held its tail still throughout the greeting.','Waggle describes repeated movement, not remaining motionless.')],[Q('waggle.q1','waggle.s1','meaning','How did the puppy move its tail?','It shook it repeatedly from side to side.','It kept it motionless.','It folded it into a wallet.','Waggle as a verb means make repeated small movements.'),Q('waggle.q2','waggle.s2','context','What did one final waggle of the handle do?','Its brief shaking loosened the tap enough for water to run.','It made the handle disappear.','It paid the plumber’s wages.','A waggle as a noun is a short shaking movement.'),Q('waggle.q3','waggle.s1','distinction','Which action is a waggle?','A child repeatedly wiggles a finger to get attention.','A child freezes a finger in one position.','A child writes a formal warning.','Repeated small motion is the key meaning.'),Q('waggle.q4','waggle.s2','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','Give the stubborn key a waggle in the lock.','Waggle the key until it turns.','The key waggles whenever she moves it.','A waggle is one short shaking movement.')]);
P('waggon','A British spelling variant of wagon; wagon is from Dutch wagen, “cart or vehicle.”',[C('waggon.s1','运货车','The museum restored a wooden waggon once used to carry coal from the mine.','博物館修復了一輛曾用來從礦場運煤的木製貨車。','a horse-drawn / railway waggon','Noun: a vehicle, especially a cart or railway car, used to carry goods.','The old vehicle transported coal.')],[M('The museum labelled the coal-carrying vehicle a waggon, then claimed that this British spelling was a different word from wagon.','The museum labelled the coal-carrying vehicle a waggon, a British spelling variant of wagon.','Waggon and wagon are spelling variants, not different headwords in meaning.')],[Q('waggon.q1','waggon.s1','meaning','What did the restored waggon carry?','Coal from a mine.','A jury’s legal decision.','A person’s clothing.','A waggon is a goods-carrying cart or railway vehicle.'),Q('waggon.q2','waggon.s1','context','Which vehicle could be called a waggon?','A horse-drawn cart carrying sacks to market.','A small hand mirror.','A passenger waiting room.','The word refers to a vehicle for carrying goods.'),Q('waggon.q3','waggon.s1','distinction','How does waggon relate to wagon?','It is a spelling variant, especially in British usage.','It names a kind of salary.','It means a different animal.','Both spellings refer to a goods vehicle.'),Q('waggon.q4','waggon.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural sentence.','The farm waggon carried hay to the barn.','The farm waggon negotiated a higher hourly wage.','The farm waggon waited for the courtroom verdict.','A vehicle can carry hay; wages and verdicts are unrelated senses.')]);
P('wagon','From Dutch wagen, “cart or vehicle”; the word names a goods vehicle, a railway car, or a station wagon in US English.',[C('wagon.s1','四轮运货车','The farmer loaded two barrels onto the wagon and drove it to the barn.','農夫把兩個木桶裝上四輪運貨車，駕車前往穀倉。','a horse-drawn / covered wagon','Noun: a four-wheeled vehicle used for carrying goods or people.','The vehicle carries barrels.'),C('wagon.s2','铁路货车','A freight wagon carrying gravel was uncoupled in the rail yard.','一節裝載碎石的鐵路貨車在調車場脫掛。','a freight / railway wagon','Noun: a railway vehicle for carrying goods.','The railway car carries gravel.'),C('wagon.s3','旅行轿车（美）','They rented a station wagon so the family and camping gear would fit.','他們租了一輛旅行轎車，讓全家和露營裝備都能放下。','a station wagon','Noun: a car with an extended rear section and a large luggage space, especially in US usage.','The family chooses a vehicle with extra cargo room.')],[M('The freight wagon carried gravel on the railway, but the report called it a passenger waiting room.','The freight wagon carried gravel on the railway.','A wagon is a vehicle, not a room for waiting passengers.')],[Q('wagon.q1','wagon.s1','meaning','What did the farmer load onto the wagon?','Two barrels.','A railway timetable.','An employee’s weekly wages.','The first sense is a four-wheeled carrying vehicle.'),Q('wagon.q2','wagon.s2','context','What was uncoupled in the rail yard?','A freight car carrying gravel.','A family’s station wagon.','A horse-drawn cart at a barn.','The railway sense is a goods-carrying rail car.'),Q('wagon.q3','wagon.s3','distinction','Why did the family rent a station wagon?','It had room for passengers and camping gear.','It was a rail car carrying gravel.','It was a horse-drawn vehicle for barrels.','A station wagon is a car with extra rear cargo space.'),Q('wagon.q4','wagon.s1','word-choice','Choose the farm-cart use.','The oxen pulled the wagon full of hay.','The train uncoupled a wagon of gravel.','The family packed the station wagon for a holiday.','The first is the general goods-cart sense.')]);
P('waif','From Anglo-French waif, “a stray or abandoned thing”; the word’s earlier origin is uncertain.',[C('waif.s1','流浪弃儿','A local shelter gave the young waif a warm meal and a safe place to sleep.','當地收容所給這名無家可歸的孩子一頓熱食和安全的睡處。','a homeless / abandoned waif','Noun: a homeless or abandoned person, especially a child.','The child lacks a home and receives shelter.')],[M('The waif was a wealthy homeowner who had never been abandoned and needed no shelter.','The waif was a homeless child who needed shelter.','A waif is an abandoned or homeless person, often a child.')],[Q('waif.q1','waif.s1','meaning','Who received help from the shelter?','A homeless young person.','A wealthy homeowner seeking investment advice.','A railway freight car.','Waif refers especially to an abandoned or homeless child.'),Q('waif.q2','waif.s1','context','Which person might a newspaper describe as a waif?','A child found alone without a home or family support.','A landlord living in a large house.','A worker negotiating an hourly wage.','The word suggests a person who is lost or abandoned.'),Q('waif.q3','waif.s1','distinction','What does the shelter provide to a waif in the example?','Safety, food, and a place to sleep.','A court verdict.','A freight wagon.','The child needs basic care and shelter.'),Q('waif.q4','waif.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','The story follows a waif searching for a safe home.','The story follows a waif who owns the shelter and rents it out.','The story follows a waif that carries coal on rails.','The first describes an abandoned or homeless person.')]);
P('wail','From Old Norse væla, “to lament”; it can describe a loud cry or the sound itself.',[C('wail.s1','哀哭（动词）','The baby began to wail when the crowded room grew too noisy.','房間變得太吵時，嬰兒開始大聲哭叫。','wail with / in + emotion','Verb: cry loudly in grief, pain, or distress.','The baby makes a loud distressed cry.'),C('wail.s2','哀号声','A distant wail of sirens crossed the valley after midnight.','午夜過後，遠處警笛的哀鳴聲傳過山谷。','a wail of + siren / grief','Noun: a long, loud cry or mournful sound.','The siren produces a drawn-out sound.')],[M('The infant wailed in distress by remaining completely silent and making no sound.','The infant showed no distress by remaining silent.','A wail is an audible loud cry, so complete silence is not a wail.')],[Q('wail.q1','wail.s1','meaning','Why did the baby wail?','The noisy room distressed the baby.','The baby was silently asleep.','The baby had won a wager.','To wail is to cry loudly from distress.'),Q('wail.q2','wail.s2','context','What crossed the valley after midnight?','A long mournful sound from distant sirens.','A railway wagon.','A quiet written warning.','A wail can be a drawn-out sound such as a siren.'),Q('wail.q3','wail.s1','distinction','Which action is wailing?','Crying out loudly after being hurt.','Whispering a calm answer.','Waiting silently in a room.','Wailing is a loud cry.'),Q('wail.q4','wail.s2','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','A wail rose from the ambulance siren.','The child wailed for several minutes.','She wails when she is upset.','The first uses wail to name the sound itself.')]);
P('waist','From Middle English waist, probably related to Old English wæst, “growth or shape”; its early history is uncertain.',[C('waist.s1','腰部','He fastened the belt around his waist before lifting the box.','搬箱子前，他把腰帶繫在腰上。','around the waist; waist measurement','Noun: the part of the body between the ribs and hips.','The belt goes around the body’s middle.'),C('waist.s2','衣服腰身','The dress has a fitted waist and a loose skirt.','這件洋裝的腰身合體，裙襬則較寬鬆。','a fitted / narrow waist','Noun: the part of a garment that covers or fits around the body’s waist.','The garment narrows at the middle.')],[M('The belt was fastened around his waist, the part of the arm between the shoulder and elbow.','The belt was fastened around his waist, the part of the body between the ribs and hips.','The waist is the body’s middle, not the upper arm.')],[Q('waist.q1','waist.s1','meaning','Where did he fasten the belt?','Around the part of the body between ribs and hips.','Around the wrist.','Around the knee.','The waist is the body’s middle.'),Q('waist.q2','waist.s2','context','What does the dress’s fitted waist describe?','The part of the garment shaped around the wearer’s middle.','The dress’s sleeve length.','The fabric’s washing instructions.','Waist can name a garment section.'),Q('waist.q3','waist.s1','distinction','Which measurement is a waist measurement?','The circumference around the middle of the torso.','The distance from shoulder to fingertip.','The length of a railway wagon.','Waist measurement is taken around the body’s middle.'),Q('waist.q4','waist.s2','word-choice','Choose the clothing use.','The coat is tailored with a narrow waist.','She felt pain in her waist after a fall.','A belt circles his waist.','The first refers to a shaped part of a garment.')]);
P('waistcoat','From waist + coat, originally a coat or garment covering the waist; today chiefly a sleeveless garment worn over a shirt.',[C('waistcoat.s1','马甲','He wore a navy waistcoat under his suit jacket for the formal dinner.','正式晚宴上，他在西裝外套裡穿了一件海軍藍馬甲。','wear / button a waistcoat','Noun: a sleeveless garment worn over a shirt, usually as part of a suit.' ,'The clothing is sleeveless and worn over a shirt.'),C('waistcoat.s2','旧式内衣','The museum display showed a nineteenth-century waistcoat worn as an undergarment.','博物館展出一件十九世紀作為內衣穿著的背心。','an old-fashioned / historical waistcoat','Noun: historically, an undershirt or garment worn next to the body.','The label describes an older clothing use.')],[M('He wore a sleeveless waistcoat over his shirt, but the sentence says it covered his feet like socks.','He wore a sleeveless waistcoat over his shirt and a pair of socks on his feet.','A waistcoat is worn on the torso, not on the feet.')],[Q('waistcoat.q1','waistcoat.s1','meaning','What did he wear beneath the suit jacket?','A sleeveless garment over his shirt.','A pair of shoes.','A railway uniform.','A waistcoat is a sleeveless upper-body garment.'),Q('waistcoat.q2','waistcoat.s2','context','What did the museum label the historical garment as?','An old-fashioned undergarment worn next to the body.','A modern freight vehicle.','A belt around the hips.','The older sense can refer to an undershirt.'),Q('waistcoat.q3','waistcoat.s1','distinction','Which outfit includes a waistcoat in its current common sense?','A shirt, waistcoat, and suit jacket.','A shirt, socks, and trousers only.','A coat worn as a shoe.','The waistcoat is the sleeveless torso layer.'),Q('waistcoat.q4','waistcoat.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural use.','He buttoned his waistcoat before putting on the jacket.','He buttoned his waistcoat around his ankle.','He drove his waistcoat down the railway line.','A waistcoat is clothing worn on the upper body.')]);
P('waistline','From waist + line; it names the body’s waist circumference or the line where clothing is shaped at the waist.',[C('waistline.s1','腰围','The tailor measured her waistline before altering the trousers.','裁縫修改長褲前量了她的腰圍。','measure / reduce the waistline','Noun: the measurement around the waist, especially the body’s circumference.' ,'The tailor measures around the wearer’s middle.'),C('waistline.s2','衣物腰线','A narrow belt emphasizes the waistline of the coat.','一條窄腰帶突顯了外套的腰線。','a high / low waistline','Noun: the line at which a garment is shaped around the waist.','The belt marks the garment’s shaped waist.')],[M('The tailor measured her waistline by measuring the length of her sleeve from shoulder to cuff.','The tailor measured her waistline by measuring around her middle.','A waistline measurement concerns the waist, not sleeve length.')],[Q('waistline.q1','waistline.s1','meaning','What did the tailor measure?','The circumference around her waist.','The distance from shoulder to cuff.','The length of a railway platform.','Waistline can mean a measurement around the middle.'),Q('waistline.q2','waistline.s2','context','What does the belt emphasize on the coat?','The line where the garment is shaped at the waist.','The coat’s sleeve opening.','The collar seam.','The clothing sense is a shaped line at the waist.'),Q('waistline.q3','waistline.s1','distinction','Which tailor’s note records a waistline measurement?','Torso circumference: 72 centimetres.','Sleeve length: 58 centimetres.','Shoulder width: 39 centimetres.','The first measures around the waist.'),Q('waistline.q4','waistline.s2','word-choice','Choose the garment-design use.','The jacket’s waistline sits just above the belt.','The patient’s waistline is 72 centimetres.','He tied the belt around his waist.','The first locates a line on a garment.')]);
P('wait','From Old North French waitier, “to watch or attend,” from a Germanic source; senses include delay, service, and the period of waiting.',[C('wait.s1','等待','We waited outside the clinic until the nurse called our number.','我們在診所外等候，直到護士叫到號碼。','wait for / wait until','Verb: stay where you are or delay action until something happens.' ,'They remain until their turn arrives.'),C('wait.s2','暂缓','Let us wait before signing until the accountant checks the figures.','我們先等一等，等會計核對數字後再簽字。','wait before doing something','Verb: delay an action until a later time.' ,'They postpone signing.'),C('wait.s3','等待时间','There was a forty-minute wait at the passport office.','護照辦公室的等候時間有四十分鐘。','a long / short wait','Noun: a period spent waiting.' ,'The phrase names the duration.'),C('wait.s4','侍候','The restaurant hired two students to wait on tables during the festival.','餐廳在節慶期間聘請兩名學生侍候餐桌。','wait on tables / customers','Verb: serve food to people at a meal or in a restaurant.' ,'The students serve diners.')],[M('We waited outside the clinic by leaving immediately before the nurse called our number.','We left the clinic before our number was called instead of waiting outside.','Waiting means remaining until an event; leaving immediately is the opposite.')],[Q('wait.q1','wait.s1','meaning','Why did they stay outside the clinic?','They were waiting for the nurse to call their number.','They were serving meals.','They had already been called and left.','Wait can mean remain until something happens.'),Q('wait.q2','wait.s2','context','Why did they wait before signing?','The accountant still needed to check the figures.','The restaurant needed another waiter.','Their forty-minute queue had ended.','This sense means delay an action.'),Q('wait.q3','wait.s3','distinction','What does “a forty-minute wait” describe?','The amount of time spent waiting.','A restaurant employee.','A signed contract.','Wait as a noun can name a period of delay.'),Q('wait.q4','wait.s4','word-choice','Which sentence uses wait to mean serve diners?','The students waited on tables during the festival.','The students waited outside until the doors opened.','The students faced a long wait at passport control.','Wait on tables means serve food to customers.')]);
P('wait for','From wait + for; the particle for marks the person or event being awaited.',[C('wait for.s1','等候','Please wait for the receptionist to call your name before entering.','請等接待員叫到你的名字後再進入。','wait for + person / thing','Phrasal verb: remain until a person or thing arrives or happens.' ,'The visitor stays until called.'),C('wait for.s2','期待','The town is waiting for the river level to fall before reopening the bridge.','小鎮正等著河水下降後再重新開放橋梁。','wait for + change / event','Phrasal verb: expect or anticipate an event.' ,'Residents expect the water to fall.')],[M('Please wait for the receptionist by entering the room before she has called you.','Please wait for the receptionist’s call before entering the room.','Entering before the call means you did not wait for it.')],[Q('wait for.q1','wait for.s1','meaning','When may the visitor enter?','After the receptionist calls the visitor’s name.','Before arriving at the reception desk.','Only after the bridge is repaired.','Wait for someone means remain until that person arrives or calls.'),Q('wait for.q2','wait for.s2','context','What is the town expecting?','The river level to fall.','A waiter to serve lunch.','A new waistcoat.','Here wait for means anticipate a future change.'),Q('wait for.q3','wait for.s1','grammar','What normally follows wait for in “wait for the bus”?','A noun naming the awaited thing.','An infinitive with no for.','A past-tense verb only.','The preposition for introduces the person or thing awaited.'),Q('wait for.q4','wait for.s2','distinction','Which sentence uses wait for in the sense of anticipate?','Scientists are waiting for the results to arrive.','We waited for the bus at the stop.','The waiter waited on the guests.','The first expresses expectation of an event.')]);
P('waiter','From wait + -er, originally “one who waits on or attends others”; it commonly names a restaurant server.',[C('waiter.s1','男侍者；服务员','The waiter brought the menu and checked whether the guests had any allergies.','服務員拿來菜單，並詢問客人是否有過敏。','ask / tip / call a waiter','Noun: a person, traditionally a man, who serves food and drinks in a restaurant.' ,'The employee attends the diners.')],[M('The waiter served the guests by refusing to take their order or bring any food.','The waiter served the guests by taking their order and bringing their meal.','A restaurant waiter serves diners rather than refusing all service.')],[Q('waiter.q1','waiter.s1','meaning','What did the waiter bring to the table?','The menu.','A freight wagon.','A jury verdict.','A waiter serves food and drinks in a restaurant.'),Q('waiter.q2','waiter.s1','context','Who should a diner call to ask about an allergy?','The restaurant server attending the table.','The person who designed the wallpaper.','The customer waiting in another room.','A waiter can answer service questions and take orders.'),Q('waiter.q3','waiter.s1','distinction','Which job is a waiter’s?','Taking orders and serving meals.','Measuring a garment waistline.','Driving a railway wagon.','The first is restaurant service.'),Q('waiter.q4','waiter.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural collocation.','leave a tip for the waiter','wage a waiter','waive a waiter','A diner may leave a tip for restaurant service.')]);
P('waiting room','A compound of waiting + room, a room provided for people who are waiting for an appointment or transport.',[C('waiting room.s1','等候室','Several patients read quietly in the waiting room before their appointments.','幾位病人在候診室裡安靜閱讀，等待看診。','sit in / enter a waiting room','Noun: a room where people stay until an appointment, service, or transport is ready.' ,'The patients wait there before being seen.')],[M('The passengers left the waiting room after boarding their train, before they had waited for it.','The passengers left the waiting room when their train was ready to board.','A waiting room is used before the awaited service or transport is ready.')],[Q('waiting room.q1','waiting room.s1','meaning','Why were the patients in the room?','They were waiting for their appointments.','They were serving meals.','They were driving a freight train.','A waiting room holds people before an appointment or service.'),Q('waiting room.q2','waiting room.s1','context','Where might passengers sit before boarding?','In a station waiting room.','In the train’s engine while it is moving.','In a restaurant kitchen.','A waiting room is a place to wait for transport.'),Q('waiting room.q3','waiting room.s1','distinction','Which room is a waiting room?','A clinic room where patients remain until called.','A bedroom where a family sleeps overnight.','A warehouse where goods are stored.','The clinic room is provided for people awaiting service.'),Q('waiting room.q4','waiting room.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural sentence.','The receptionist directed the early arrivals to the waiting room.','The receptionist served lunch in the waiting room to the train.','The receptionist measured the waiting room’s waistline.','People can be directed to a room while they await an appointment.')]);
P('waitress','From wait + -ress, a traditional feminine agent noun for a person serving food; waiter is often used gender-neutrally today.',[C('waitress.s1','女侍者；服务员','The waitress explained which dishes contained peanuts before taking the order.','女服務員在點餐前說明哪些菜含有花生。','ask / tip / call a waitress','Noun: a woman who serves food and drinks in a restaurant.' ,'She attends customers and answers a question about the menu.')],[M('The waitress took the guests’ order by refusing to speak with them and leaving the table.','The waitress took the guests’ order by asking what they would like to eat.','Taking an order requires attending to the guests rather than refusing contact.')],[Q('waitress.q1','waitress.s1','meaning','What information did the waitress provide?','Which dishes contained peanuts.','How much the guests earned in wages.','Where the railway wagon was stored.','A waitress serves diners and can answer menu questions.'),Q('waitress.q2','waitress.s1','context','Who takes a restaurant customer’s food order in this example?','The woman serving the table.','A patient in the waiting room.','A passenger in a wagon.','The waitress is the restaurant server.'),Q('waitress.q3','waitress.s1','distinction','Which task belongs to a waitress?','Bringing dishes to restaurant customers.','Issuing a court verdict.','Repairing wallpaper.','The first is a restaurant-service task.'),Q('waitress.q4','waitress.s1','usage','Which statement about the word is accurate?','Waitress traditionally names a woman server; waiter is also often gender-neutral.','Waitress names any waiting room.','Waitress is the plural form of wages.','The word has a traditional feminine agent ending.')]);
P('waive','From Anglo-French weyver, “abandon or give up”; it commonly means relinquish a right or choose not to enforce a fee or rule.',[C('waive.s1','放弃权利','The witness agreed to waive the right to remain anonymous.','證人同意放棄保持匿名的權利。','waive a right / claim / privilege','Verb: voluntarily give up a right, claim, or privilege.' ,'The witness relinquishes anonymity protection.'),C('waive.s2','免收；不执行','The university waived the application fee for students with financial need.','大學為有經濟困難的學生免除了申請費。','waive a fee / requirement / rule','Verb: decide not to demand or enforce a fee, requirement, or rule.' ,'The university chooses not to collect the fee.')],[M('The university waived the application fee by charging every applicant the full amount.','The university collected the application fee from every applicant.','Waive a fee means choose not to charge it, not collect it.')],[Q('waive.q1','waive.s1','meaning','What did the witness give up?','The right to remain anonymous.','A restaurant table.','A railway ticket.','Waive can mean relinquish a right or privilege.'),Q('waive.q2','waive.s2','context','What did the university do for some applicants?','It chose not to charge them the application fee.','It required them to pay twice.','It made them wait for a verdict.','Waive a fee means not demand payment.'),Q('waive.q3','waive.s1','distinction','Which action waives a right?','A person voluntarily gives up the right to appeal.','A person insists on using the right to appeal.','A person pays a restaurant bill.','Waive here means relinquish a legal right.'),Q('waive.q4','waive.s2','word-choice','Choose the fee-related use.','The clinic waived the charge for the follow-up visit.','The witness waived the right to privacy.','The court issued a warrant.','The first means the clinic did not collect a fee.')]);
P('wake','From Old English wacan, “be awake,” with related senses of rousing, a funeral gathering, and a ship’s trailing wave.',[C('wake.s1','醒来','I usually wake before sunrise when the room begins to brighten.','房間開始變亮時，我通常在日出前醒來。','wake early / from sleep','Verb: stop sleeping and become conscious.' ,'The person becomes awake.'),C('wake.s2','叫醒','Please wake the children gently before the alarm sounds.','鬧鐘響起前，請輕輕叫醒孩子們。','wake someone; wake up','Verb: cause someone to stop sleeping.' ,'The speaker causes the children to become awake.'),C('wake.s3','唤起','The documentary may wake public interest in the history of the harbor.','這部紀錄片可能喚起公眾對港口歷史的興趣。','wake interest / memories','Verb: cause a feeling, memory, or awareness to become active.' ,'The film brings interest into awareness.'),C('wake.s4','守灵聚会','Relatives held a quiet wake after the funeral, sharing stories about their uncle.','葬禮後，親戚舉行了安靜的守靈聚會，分享叔叔的故事。','hold / attend a wake','Noun: a gathering associated with the time before or after a funeral.' ,'Family and friends gather to remember the deceased.'),C('wake.s5','船尾波浪','The kayak rocked gently in the wake of the ferry.','獨木舟在渡輪留下的尾波中輕輕搖晃。','in the wake of a ship / boat','Noun: the waves or track left behind by a moving ship; also a following result.','The ferry leaves waves behind it.')],[M('The kayak was in the ferry’s wake while floating several miles ahead of the ferry.','The kayak was in the ferry’s wake while floating behind it.','A vessel’s wake trails behind the moving vessel.')],[Q('wake.q1','wake.s1','meaning','What happens when the speaker wakes before sunrise?','The speaker stops sleeping and becomes conscious.','The speaker hosts a funeral gathering.','The speaker leaves waves behind a boat.','Wake in this sense means stop sleeping.'),Q('wake.q2','wake.s2','context','What does the speaker do to the children?','Causes them to stop sleeping.','Waits for them to arrive at a clinic.','Waves behind their boat.','Wake someone is to rouse that person.'),Q('wake.q3','wake.s3','distinction','What may the documentary wake?','Public interest in harbor history.','The children from sleep.','A ferry’s trailing waves.','This figurative sense activates awareness or interest.'),Q('wake.q4','wake.s5','word-choice','What rocked the kayak?','Waves left behind by a passing ferry.','A funeral gathering.','A sleeper becoming conscious.','A ship’s wake is the water disturbed behind it.')]);
P('wake up','From wake + up, a phrasal verb meaning become awake or cause someone to become awake.',[C('wake up.s1','醒来','She woke up before dawn and heard rain tapping against the window.','她黎明前醒來，聽見雨點敲打窗戶。','wake up early / suddenly','Phrasal verb: stop sleeping and become fully conscious.' ,'She becomes awake before dawn.'),C('wake up.s2','叫醒','The caretaker woke up the guard when smoke appeared near the kitchen.','廚房附近冒煙時，管理員叫醒了警衛。','wake someone up','Phrasal verb: cause someone to stop sleeping.' ,'The caretaker rouses the sleeping guard.')],[M('The caretaker woke the guard up by keeping him asleep and preventing him from becoming conscious.','The caretaker kept the guard asleep and did not wake him up.','To wake someone up is to make that person stop sleeping.')],[Q('wake up.q1','wake up.s1','meaning','What did she do before dawn?','She stopped sleeping and became conscious.','She held a funeral gathering.','She left a boat’s wake.','Wake up can mean become awake.'),Q('wake up.q2','wake up.s2','context','Why did the caretaker rouse the guard?','Smoke appeared near the kitchen.','The guard had to serve dinner.','The ferry was waiting at a station.','Wake someone up means cause them to wake.'),Q('wake up.q3','wake up.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses wake up without an object?','I woke up when the alarm rang.','I woke my brother before sunrise.','The ferry left a wake behind it.','The subject becomes awake; no person is directly woken.'),Q('wake up.q4','wake up.s2','grammar','Where can the object go in “wake the guard up”?','Between wake and up, or after wake up.','Only before wake, with no other option.','Only after the sentence ends.','This separable phrasal verb allows “wake the guard up” and “wake up the guard.”')]);
P('waken','From Old English wacian, “be awake or become awake”; it can mean become awake or cause another person to wake.',[C('waken.s1','唤醒','The smell of coffee wakened the travelers before the guide arrived.','導遊抵達前，咖啡香喚醒了旅人。','waken someone from sleep','Verb: cause someone to stop sleeping.' ,'The smell rouses the travelers.'),C('waken.s2','醒来','He wakened at the first light and began packing for the hike.','天剛亮他就醒來，開始為健行收拾行李。','waken at / from sleep','Verb: become awake after sleeping.' ,'He comes out of sleep at daybreak.')],[M('The coffee aroma wakened the travelers by making them fall into a deeper sleep.','The coffee aroma left the travelers asleep instead of waking them.','Waken means cause someone to become awake, not make them sleep more deeply.')],[Q('waken.q1','waken.s1','meaning','What did the coffee smell do?','It caused the travelers to wake.','It sent the travelers into deeper sleep.','It delayed their wages.','Waken in the transitive sense means rouse someone.'),Q('waken.q2','waken.s2','context','When did he become awake?','At the first light of day.','After the hike had ended.','When the train left its station.','Waken can mean become awake.'),Q('waken.q3','waken.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses waken to affect another person?','The alarm wakened the children.','The children wakened before dawn.','The dawn wakened slowly over the hills.','The alarm is the cause that wakes someone.'),Q('waken.q4','waken.s2','word-choice','Choose the intransitive use.','She wakened at dawn without an alarm.','The bell wakened the sleeping dog.','The smell wakened the travelers.','In the first, she herself becomes awake.')]);
P('wale','From Old English walu, “ridge or raised mark”; it names a raised welt or stripe and can mean strike so as to raise a welt.',[C('wale.s1','隆起伤痕','A narrow wale remained on his arm where the tight strap had pressed the skin.','緊繃的帶子壓過皮膚後，他手臂上留下一道隆起的傷痕。','a red / raised wale','Noun: a raised mark or welt on the skin.' ,'The strap has left a raised line.'),C('wale.s2','布面凸条','The corduroy jacket has fine wales running lengthwise down each sleeve.','這件燈芯絨外套的袖子上有細密的縱向凸條。','fine / broad wales in cloth','Noun: a raised ridge or stripe in woven fabric.' ,'The fabric surface has parallel ridges.'),C('wale.s3','抽打','The old story says the guard waled the thief with a leather strap.','這則舊故事說，看守用皮帶抽打了小偷。','wale someone with + object','Verb: beat or strike so as to raise a welt.' ,'The strap is used to strike the person.')],[M('The corduroy had smooth, flat cloth with no raised stripes, yet the tailor called each ridge a wale.','The corduroy had raised stripes, each of which was a wale.','A wale in fabric is a raised ridge or stripe, not a perfectly flat area.')],[Q('wale.q1','wale.s1','meaning','What remained on his arm?','A raised mark where the strap pressed.','A railway freight car.','A verse from a song.','A skin wale is a raised welt.'),Q('wale.q2','wale.s2','context','What did the tailor notice on the corduroy?','Raised ridges running along the fabric.','A perfectly smooth surface with no lines.','A person’s waist measurement.','A cloth wale is a raised stripe or ridge.'),Q('wale.q3','wale.s3','distinction','What did the guard do with the strap in the story?','Struck the thief hard enough to raise a welt.','Used it to sew parallel cloth ridges.','Measured the thief’s sleeve.','Wale as a verb means beat so as to leave a welt.'),Q('wale.q4','wale.s2','word-choice','Choose the fabric use.','The sweater’s knitted wales formed vertical ridges.','The strap left a wale on his skin.','The guard waled the prisoner.','The first describes raised textile ridges.')]);
P('walk','From Old English wealcan, “roll or toss,” later “move on foot”; senses include guiding someone, a stroll, and a path.',[C('walk.s1','步行','We walked through the old market before the shops opened.','商店開門前，我們步行穿過老市場。','walk to / through / along','Verb: move forward on foot at a regular pace.' ,'They travel by walking.'),C('walk.s2','带着走','She walks her dog beside the canal every morning.','她每天早上沿著運河遛狗。','walk a dog / child home','Verb: take or guide someone or an animal on foot.' ,'She accompanies the dog along a route.'),C('walk.s3','散步','We took a short walk after dinner to enjoy the cool air.','晚餐後我們短暫散步，享受涼爽的空氣。','take / go for a walk','Noun: a journey or period of walking.' ,'The phrase names an outing on foot.'),C('walk.s4','步道','A wooden walk leads visitors across the marsh without damaging the plants.','一條木棧道引領遊客穿過沼澤，不會破壞植物。','a boardwalk / public walk','Noun: a path intended for people to walk along.' ,'The structure is a pedestrian path.')],[M('They walked across the market by remaining in one place and never moving their feet.','They stayed still in the market instead of walking across it.','Walking requires movement on foot.')],[Q('walk.q1','walk.s1','meaning','How did the visitors cross the market?','They moved through it on foot.','They drove a railway wagon through it.','They waited without moving.','Walk as a verb means move forward on foot.'),Q('walk.q2','walk.s2','context','What does she do with her dog each morning?','She takes it along the canal on foot.','She leaves it alone at home.','She measures its waistline.','Walk an animal means guide it on a walk.'),Q('walk.q3','walk.s3','distinction','What did they take after dinner?','A short stroll.','A jury’s verdict.','A train ticket.','A walk as a noun is a period or trip on foot.'),Q('walk.q4','walk.s4','word-choice','Which sentence names a path?','The raised walk crosses the marsh.','They walk across the marsh each day.','They took a walk after lunch.','Here walk is a constructed route.')]);
P('walk out','From walk + out; it can mean leave a place or abandon work or cooperation as a protest.',[C('walk out.s1','走出；离开','She walked out of the meeting after the chair refused to hear her evidence.','主席拒絕聽取她的證據後，她走出了會議。','walk out of + room / meeting','Phrasal verb: leave a place, often suddenly or in protest.' ,'She exits the meeting.'),C('walk out.s2','罢工；退出合作','Dockworkers walked out for two days to demand safer equipment.','碼頭工人罷工兩天，要求更安全的設備。','workers walk out; walk out on + employer','Phrasal verb: stop working or withdraw cooperation as a protest.' ,'The workers suspend their labor action.')],[M('The dockworkers walked out for a two-day strike while continuing every shift without interruption.','The dockworkers stayed at work instead of walking out on strike.','A walkout means workers stop work; uninterrupted shifts contradict a strike.')],[Q('walk out.q1','walk out.s1','meaning','What did she do after her evidence was rejected?','She left the meeting.','She began serving tables.','She measured a path.','Walk out of a place means leave it.'),Q('walk out.q2','walk out.s2','context','Why did the dockworkers stop work?','To protest and demand safer equipment.','To take a short stroll after dinner.','To wait for their train.','The labor sense is a strike or withdrawal of cooperation.'),Q('walk out.q3','walk out.s1','distinction','Which action is a literal walkout from a room?','A guest rises and leaves the hall during the discussion.','Workers refuse all shifts for two days.','A guard walks a dog.','The first is physically leaving a place.'),Q('walk out.q4','walk out.s2','word-choice','Choose the labor-protest use.','The nurses walked out over unsafe staffing levels.','She walked out of the cinema after the film ended.','He walked out to the garden for fresh air.','The nurses stop working in protest.')]);
P('walker','From walk + -er, a person who walks; it can also refer to a competitor in race walking.',[C('walker.s1','步行者','A walker on the coastal path stopped to watch dolphins offshore.','一位沿海岸步道散步的人停下來觀看近海的海豚。','a brisk / long-distance walker','Noun: a person who travels on foot for exercise or pleasure.' ,'The person is walking for recreation.'),C('walker.s2','竞走运动员','The race walker kept one foot in contact with the track during each stride.','這名競走運動員每一步都讓一隻腳保持接觸跑道。','a competitive / Olympic walker','Noun: an athlete who competes in race walking.' ,'The athlete follows the race-walking technique.')],[M('The walker won the race-walking event while running every section with both feet off the track.','The runner won the event by running; a race walker must maintain the required walking action.','Running with both feet airborne violates race-walking technique.')],[Q('walker.q1','walker.s1','meaning','Why did the person stop on the coastal path?','To watch dolphins while out on foot.','To serve food in a restaurant.','To inspect a railway wagon.','A walker can be someone walking for pleasure.'),Q('walker.q2','walker.s2','context','What did the athlete maintain during each stride?','At least one foot remained in contact with the track.','Both feet were airborne at once.','The athlete rode in a wagon.','A race walker follows the event’s walking technique.'),Q('walker.q3','walker.s1','distinction','Which person is a recreational walker?','Someone taking a long footpath stroll.','An athlete in a sprint race.','A waiter carrying plates.','The first person walks for exercise or pleasure.'),Q('walker.q4','walker.s2','word-choice','Choose the race-sport use.','The Olympic walker trained for the 20-kilometre event.','The walker explored the coastal trail at a leisurely pace.','A walker waited in the clinic.','The first names a race-walking athlete.')]);
P('walking','From walk + -ing; it names the activity of walking and can describe a journey made on foot.',[C('walking.s1','步行；散步','Walking after lunch helps me clear my mind before the afternoon meeting.','午餐後散步有助於我在下午會議前整理思緒。','go / take up walking','Noun: the activity of moving on foot for exercise or travel.' ,'Walking is the activity being discussed.'),C('walking.s2','步行的','They followed a walking route that linked the station to three historic gardens.','他們沿著一條步行路線，從車站連接到三座歷史花園。','a walking route / holiday','Adjective: involving travel or movement on foot.' ,'The route is designed for people on foot.')],[M('They chose a walking route that could be completed only by driving a car and never leaving it.','They chose a driving route that could be completed by car.','A walking route is intended for travel on foot, not exclusively by car.')],[Q('walking.q1','walking.s1','meaning','What activity helps clear the speaker’s mind?','Moving on foot after lunch.','Driving through the city.','Serving meals at a café.','Walking as a noun is the activity of going on foot.'),Q('walking.q2','walking.s2','context','How do visitors travel along the garden route?','On foot.','Only by freight train.','By remaining seated in a car.','The adjective describes a route intended for walking.'),Q('walking.q3','walking.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses walking as a noun?','Walking is part of her daily exercise.','They chose a walking tour of the gardens.','The walking route starts at the station.','In the first, walking names the activity.'),Q('walking.q4','walking.s2','word-choice','Choose the adjectival use.','A walking map marks paths between villages.','Walking in the hills can be tiring.','She enjoys walking before breakfast.','The first modifies map and describes a foot-travel route.')]);
P('walkout','From walk out, a compound naming the act of leaving together, especially as a protest or strike.',[C('walkout.s1','集体离场；罢工','The students staged a walkout to protest the closure of the language program.','學生集體離場抗議語言課程被關閉。','stage / organize / join a walkout','Noun: a coordinated act of leaving a workplace or event, usually in protest.' ,'The students leave together to make a protest.')],[M('The workers’ walkout consisted of staying at their desks and continuing the same work without protest.','The workers’ meeting continued at their desks; there was no walkout.','A walkout involves leaving or stopping work, not continuing normally.')],[Q('walkout.q1','walkout.s1','meaning','Why did the students leave together?','To protest the program’s closure.','To take a routine walk after lunch.','To enter a waiting room.','A walkout is a coordinated protest departure or strike.'),Q('walkout.q2','walkout.s1','context','Which situation is a walkout?','Employees leave the factory floor together during a labor dispute.','One employee quietly walks a dog.','A guest arrives early for a meeting.','The coordinated departure signals a protest.'),Q('walkout.q3','walkout.s1','distinction','How does a walkout differ from an ordinary break?','It is organized as a protest or labor action.','It always happens outdoors.','It means a person takes a daily walk.','The protest purpose distinguishes a walkout.'),Q('walkout.q4','walkout.s1','word-choice','Choose the protest noun.','The nurses’ walkout lasted until management reopened negotiations.','The nurse walked out of the room to answer a call.','The nurse walks her dog after work.','The first names a coordinated labor action.')]);
P('walkway','From walk + way, a route or passage made for people on foot.',[C('walkway.s1','走道','A covered walkway connects the library to the science building.','一條有頂走道連接圖書館和科學大樓。','a covered / pedestrian walkway','Noun: a path or passage for people walking.' ,'The structure lets pedestrians travel between buildings.')],[M('The covered walkway was a route for cars only and had no space for pedestrians.','The covered roadway was a route for cars only and had no space for pedestrians.','A walkway is intended for people walking, not cars only.')],[Q('walkway.q1','walkway.s1','meaning','What does the covered structure connect?','The library and the science building.','Two railway wagons.','A courtroom and a restaurant.','A walkway is a passage for pedestrians.'),Q('walkway.q2','walkway.s1','context','Which feature identifies a walkway?','It provides a route for people on foot.','It is reserved for cars only.','It is a room where passengers wait.','The word names a pedestrian path.'),Q('walkway.q3','walkway.s1','distinction','Where would pedestrians likely use a walkway?','Across a bridge between two campus buildings.','Inside a moving freight car.','Around a garment’s waistline.','The bridge passage is built for people walking.'),Q('walkway.q4','walkway.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural use.','A lit walkway runs from the station to the terminal.','The lit walkway paid every employee a weekly wage.','The lit walkway returned the jury’s verdict.','A walkway can connect pedestrian destinations.')]);
P('wall','From Old English weall, from Latin vallum, “rampart”; it names a physical barrier, an obstacle, or the act of enclosing with walls.',[C('wall.s1','墙壁','A crack appeared in the wall beside the kitchen window.','廚房窗戶旁的牆上出現一道裂縫。','a brick / interior wall','Noun: a vertical structure forming part of a building or room.' ,'The crack is in the building structure.'),C('wall.s2','围墙','A stone wall surrounds the old garden and keeps deer out.','一道石圍牆環繞著老花園，阻擋鹿群進入。','a boundary / garden wall','Noun: a structure built around an area for protection or division.' ,'The wall encloses the garden.'),C('wall.s3','障碍','Lack of funding became a wall between the proposal and its completion.','資金不足成了提案與完成之間的障礙。','a wall between / against progress','Noun: a barrier or obstacle, literal or figurative.' ,'The shortage prevents progress.'),C('wall.s4','用墙围住','They walled the narrow courtyard to keep the livestock out.','他們築牆圍住狹窄庭院，以免牲畜進入。','wall off / wall in an area','Verb: enclose or separate a place by building a wall.' ,'The courtyard is enclosed.')],[M('The garden wall protected the plants by leaving the garden completely open to deer.','The garden wall protected the plants by enclosing the garden and keeping deer out.','A boundary wall cannot keep deer out if it leaves the area open.')],[Q('wall.q1','wall.s1','meaning','Where did the crack appear?','In a vertical part of the kitchen structure.','In a weekly paycheck.','In the middle of a river’s wake.','Wall can name a building’s vertical structure.'),Q('wall.q2','wall.s2','context','What does the stone wall do around the garden?','Encloses it and keeps deer out.','Connects two buildings as a walkway.','Provides a place for a jury to meet.','A boundary wall divides or protects an area.'),Q('wall.q3','wall.s3','distinction','What did the lack of funding become?','An obstacle to completing the proposal.','A wall made from bricks in a courtyard.','A garment’s waistline.','The figurative sense is a barrier to progress.'),Q('wall.q4','wall.s4','grammar','What does “They walled off the courtyard” mean?','They enclosed or separated it with a wall.','They painted wallpaper inside it.','They walked out of it.','The verb wall off means enclose or isolate a place.')]);
P('wallet','From Middle English wallet, from Anglo-Norman walet, a small bag or pouch; it now means a pocket case for money or a digital payment account.',[C('wallet.s1','钱包','She put the receipt back in her leather wallet and zipped her bag.','她把收據放回皮夾，然後拉上包包拉鍊。','a leather / billfold wallet','Noun: a small flat case for carrying money, cards, or documents.' ,'The case holds a receipt and other small items.'),C('wallet.s2','电子钱包','The customer added a transit pass to the mobile wallet on her phone.','顧客把交通卡加入手機上的電子錢包。','a digital / mobile wallet','Noun: an electronic account or application used to store payment information.' ,'The phone stores payment credentials.')],[M('She paid with her wallet by leaving all cash and cards at home and using no digital payment account.','She paid with her mobile wallet, which stored her payment information.','A physical wallet or digital wallet must be used to carry or access payment details.')],[Q('wallet.q1','wallet.s1','meaning','Where did she put the receipt?','In a small case for money and cards.','In a freight wagon.','In a courtroom file.','A wallet is a small case for carrying personal items.'),Q('wallet.q2','wallet.s2','context','What did the customer add to her phone?','A transit pass in a digital payment application.','A paper wall covering.','A garden boundary.','A mobile wallet stores digital payment information.'),Q('wallet.q3','wallet.s1','distinction','Which wallet is a physical object?','A leather case kept in a jacket pocket.','A payment app on a phone.','A railway carriage.','The leather case is a physical wallet.'),Q('wallet.q4','wallet.s2','word-choice','Choose the digital-payment use.','He tapped the phone’s wallet to pay for the ticket.','He took cash from the wallet in his pocket.','He left his wallet on the restaurant table.','The first refers to an electronic wallet app.')]);
P('wallpaper','From wall + paper, paper used as a decorative covering for interior walls.',[C('wallpaper.s1','墙纸','They chose pale green wallpaper with a subtle leaf pattern for the bedroom.','他們為臥室挑選了淡綠色、帶有細緻葉片圖案的壁紙。','hang / remove / patterned wallpaper','Noun: decorative paper fixed to the inside walls of a room.' ,'The paper covers and decorates the room’s walls.')],[M('They decorated the wall with wallpaper by leaving it bare and applying no covering.','They decorated the wall with paint and left off the wallpaper.','A bare, uncovered wall has no wallpaper.')],[Q('wallpaper.q1','wallpaper.s1','meaning','What did they choose for the bedroom walls?','Decorative paper with a leaf pattern.','A leather wallet.','A wooden walkway.','Wallpaper is paper used to cover and decorate interior walls.'),Q('wallpaper.q2','wallpaper.s1','context','What would a decorator do with wallpaper?','Paste it onto an interior wall.','Use it to pay for a ticket.','Hang it from a garden wall as a wage notice.','Wallpaper is fixed to room walls.'),Q('wallpaper.q3','wallpaper.s1','distinction','Which is wallpaper rather than paint?','A patterned paper sheet covering the wall.','A coloured liquid brushed onto the wall.','A curtain covering a window.','Wallpaper is a paper wall covering.'),Q('wallpaper.q4','wallpaper.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','strip the old wallpaper before decorating','strip the old wallet before decorating','strip the old wage before decorating','Wallpaper is a covering that can be removed from a wall.')]);
P('walnut','From Old English wealhhnutu, “foreign nut,” from wealh, “foreign,” + hnutu, “nut.”',[C('walnut.s1','核桃','Chopped walnut added a rich crunch to the pear salad.','切碎的核桃為梨子沙拉增添了濃郁酥脆的口感。','a walnut tree / kernel / shell','Noun: the edible nut of a walnut tree, usually with a hard wrinkled shell.' ,'The chopped nut adds texture to the salad.')],[M('She sprinkled walnut over the salad, but the ingredient was a hard-shelled nut from a walnut tree, not a leafy herb.','She sprinkled chopped walnut over the salad, using the edible nut rather than a herb.','A walnut is a nut, not an herb.')],[Q('walnut.q1','walnut.s1','meaning','What did the chopped walnut add to the salad?','A rich crunchy texture.','A paper wall covering.','A metal fastening.','Walnut is an edible nut.'),Q('walnut.q2','walnut.s1','context','What grows on a walnut tree?','Nuts with hard, wrinkled shells.','Small leather wallets.','Railway wagons.','The tree produces walnuts.'),Q('walnut.q3','walnut.s1','distinction','Which ingredient is a walnut?','The edible kernel from a hard-shelled tree nut.','A leafy culinary herb.','A type of fabric stripe.','Walnut is the nut or its edible kernel.'),Q('walnut.q4','walnut.s1','word-choice','Choose the food use.','The baker folded chopped walnuts into the batter.','The baker folded wallpaper into the batter.','The baker folded wages into the batter.','Walnuts are edible nuts used in cooking.')]);
P('walrus','From Dutch walrus, perhaps from a North Germanic source; it names a large Arctic marine mammal and, figuratively, a walrus-like moustache.',[C('walrus.s1','海象','A walrus hauled itself onto the ice beside the breathing hole.','一頭海象把身體拖上呼吸孔旁的冰面。','an Arctic walrus; a herd of walruses','Noun: a large Arctic sea mammal with tusks and whiskers.' ,'The animal rests on sea ice.'),C('walrus.s2','海象胡子（比喻）','The actor wore a thick walrus that covered his upper lip for the period role.','這名演員為了年代角色留著厚厚的海象式鬍子，遮住上唇。','a walrus moustache','Noun: informal, a thick drooping moustache resembling a walrus’s whiskers.' ,'The moustache hangs over the upper lip.')],[M('The Arctic walrus was a small desert insect with no tusks or whiskers.','The Arctic walrus was a large marine mammal with tusks and whiskers.','A walrus is an Arctic marine mammal, not a desert insect.')],[Q('walrus.q1','walrus.s1','meaning','What animal climbed onto the ice?','A large Arctic mammal with tusks and whiskers.','A desert insect.','A railway carriage.','A walrus is an Arctic sea mammal.'),Q('walrus.q2','walrus.s2','context','What did the actor wear?','A thick moustache hanging over the upper lip.','A pair of tusks.','A leather waistcoat.','Walrus can informally describe a walrus-style moustache.'),Q('walrus.q3','walrus.s1','distinction','Where would a walrus naturally live?','In Arctic marine environments.','In a hot desert far from water.','In a restaurant waiting room.','Walruses are Arctic marine mammals.'),Q('walrus.q4','walrus.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative grooming use.','He grew a walrus moustache for the theatre role.','A walrus hauled out on the sea ice.','The walrus dived beneath the Arctic water.','The first refers to the moustache style.')]);
P('wan','From Old English wann, “dark, pale, or gloomy”; it describes an unusually pale or sick-looking appearance.',[C('wan.s1','苍白憔悴','After the long fever, he looked wan but was glad to sit up and speak.','長時間發燒後，他看起來蒼白憔悴，但很高興能坐起來說話。','look / grow wan','Adjective: pale and unhealthy-looking, often from illness or tiredness.' ,'His face appears pale after the fever.')],[M('After the fever, he looked wan with a bright, ruddy complexion and vigorous health.','After the fever, he looked healthy with a bright, ruddy complexion.','A wan appearance is pale or sick-looking, not ruddy and vigorous.')],[Q('wan.q1','wan.s1','meaning','How did he look after the fever?','Pale and tired.','Bright red and full of energy.','Ready to serve a meal.','Wan describes a pale, unhealthy-looking appearance.'),Q('wan.q2','wan.s1','context','Which person looks wan?','Someone whose face has turned pale after a long illness.','Someone with a healthy flushed face after exercise.','Someone standing beside a wall.','The adjective suggests pallor or weakness.'),Q('wan.q3','wan.s1','distinction','What contrast best explains wan?','Pale and weary rather than healthy and rosy.','Loud rather than quiet.','Vertical rather than horizontal.','Wan describes appearance and mood, often pallor.'),Q('wan.q4','wan.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate sentence.','Her wan face showed how little she had slept.','Her wan face glowed with a deep, healthy tan.','Her wan face was a railway wagon.','The first naturally uses wan for a tired pale appearance.')]);
P('wand','From Old English wand, “rod or slender stick”; it can mean a thin stick used by a magician or as a tool.',[C('wand.s1','细棒；魔杖','The stage magician tapped the empty box with a silver wand.','舞台魔術師用銀色魔杖敲了敲空盒子。','a magic / conductor’s wand','Noun: a thin stick used by a magician or as a tool for directing or applying something.' ,'The magician holds and taps with a slender stick.')],[M('The magician waved a wand, which was a thick stone wall built across the stage.','The magician waved a thin wand across the stage.','A wand is a slender rod, not a wall.')],[Q('wand.q1','wand.s1','meaning','What did the magician tap on the box?','A thin silver rod.','A paper covering.','A garden fence.','A wand is a slender stick or rod.'),Q('wand.q2','wand.s1','context','Which object could be a wand?','A narrow stick used to direct a choir.','A broad brick wall.','A leather wallet.','A wand can be used to direct or apply something.'),Q('wand.q3','wand.s1','distinction','How is a wand different from a wall?','It is a thin handheld stick.','It is a large fixed barrier.','It is a room where people wait.','A wand is a slender rod.'),Q('wand.q4','wand.s1','word-choice','Choose the magical use.','She raised her wand and the stage lights dimmed.','She raised her wallpaper and the lights dimmed.','She raised her wage and the lights dimmed.','A magician raises or waves a wand.')]);
P('wander','From Old English wandrian, “move aimlessly or stray”; it also describes thoughts straying and can be a noun for a leisurely walk.',[C('wander.s1','漫步；闲逛','We wandered through the harbor market without choosing a particular route.','我們沒有選定路線，在港口市集裡隨意閒逛。','wander around / through','Verb: walk or travel with no fixed direction or purpose.' ,'They move around without a set route.'),C('wander.s2','走失；偏离','The hikers wandered off the marked trail when the fog covered the signs.','霧氣遮住標誌後，健行者偏離了標記步道。','wander off / from a path','Verb: move away from the correct route or subject.' ,'They stray from the trail.'),C('wander.s3','走神','My mind began to wander during the long lecture, and I missed the next instruction.','冗長的演講中，我開始走神，錯過了下一條指示。','mind / attention wanders','Verb: let the thoughts move away from the matter in hand.' ,'Attention shifts away from the lecture.'),C('wander.s4','漫步','After dinner, we went for a wander along the river.','晚飯後，我們沿著河邊散步。','go for a wander','Noun: a walk or journey with no particular direction.' ,'The phrase names an unplanned stroll.')],[M('The hikers wandered off the trail by following every sign exactly and staying on the marked route.','The hikers stayed on the trail by following the signs exactly.','Wandering off means straying from the marked route.')],[Q('wander.q1','wander.s1','meaning','How did they explore the market?','They walked around without a fixed route.','They followed one marked trail.','They remained seated in a waiting room.','Wander can mean move around aimlessly.'),Q('wander.q2','wander.s2','context','Why did the hikers become lost?','They strayed from the marked trail in the fog.','They stayed on every signposted path.','They walked around the harbor market.','Wander off means leave the intended route.'),Q('wander.q3','wander.s3','distinction','What happened during the lecture?','The speaker’s attention drifted away from the topic.','The speaker walked off a trail.','The speaker took a stroll along a river.','A mind can wander when attention strays.'),Q('wander.q4','wander.s4','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','They took a quiet wander along the river after dinner.','They wandered around the harbor market.','Their minds wandered during the lecture.','The first uses wander as a noun meaning stroll.')]);
P('wanderer','From wander + -er, a person who travels without a fixed home or route.',[C('wanderer.s1','流浪者','The novel’s wanderer moved from town to town, carrying only a small pack.','小說中的流浪者背著小背包，從一個城鎮走到另一個城鎮。','a homeless / solitary wanderer','Noun: a person who travels from place to place, often without a fixed home.' ,'The person has no settled destination.'),C('wanderer.s2','漫游者','The park ranger found a wanderer who had lost the trail but still had enough water.','公園巡護員找到一名偏離步道的漫遊者，他的水仍足夠。','a wanderer in the hills / woods','Noun: someone who roams or walks about without a fixed route.' ,'The person is roaming in the area.')],[M('The wanderer never left his fixed home or travelled to any other place.','The settled resident never left his fixed home or travelled to another place.','A wanderer roams or travels rather than remaining permanently in one place.')],[Q('wanderer.q1','wanderer.s1','meaning','How did the novel’s wanderer travel?','From town to town with few possessions.','By staying forever in one house.','By working as a restaurant server.','A wanderer may travel without a settled home.'),Q('wanderer.q2','wanderer.s2','context','Why did the ranger find the person?','The person had roamed away from the trail.','The person was waiting in the clinic.','The person had built a wall.','A wanderer can be someone roaming without a fixed route.'),Q('wanderer.q3','wanderer.s1','distinction','Which person is a wanderer?','A traveler who moves between places without a settled address.','A person who never leaves one home.','A commuter who takes the same bus daily.','The first has no fixed home or route.'),Q('wanderer.q4','wanderer.s2','word-choice','Choose the roaming-person use.','A wanderer explored the forest paths all afternoon.','The wanderer negotiated a weekly wage at the factory.','The wanderer served the dinner guests.','The first describes someone walking about.')]);
P('wandering','From wander + -ing, describing movement without a fixed route or direction.',[C('wandering.s1','徘徊的；漫游的','A wandering dog appeared at the farm gate after the storm.','暴風雨後，一隻徘徊的狗出現在農場大門口。','a wandering animal / path / gaze','Adjective: moving about without a fixed direction or route.' ,'The dog has no clear route or owner nearby.')],[M('The wandering dog stayed at the same marked spot for years and never moved at all.','The stationary dog stayed at the same marked spot for years and never moved.','Something wandering moves about rather than staying fixed.')],[Q('wandering.q1','wandering.s1','meaning','What kind of dog appeared at the gate?','One moving about without a fixed route.','One that had never moved from a fixed spot.','One trained to serve food.','Wandering describes movement without a set direction.'),Q('wandering.q2','wandering.s1','context','Which gaze is wandering?','A person’s eyes drift from one part of the room to another.','A person’s eyes remain fixed on one point.','A person’s eyes are closed in sleep.','A wandering gaze shifts about.'),Q('wandering.q3','wandering.s1','distinction','What contrasts with a wandering path?','A straight route that stays fixed and direct.','A trail that twists without a set course.','A person roaming between towns.','The first is fixed and direct rather than wandering.'),Q('wandering.q4','wandering.s1','word-choice','Choose the adjectival use.','A wandering stream changed course across the plain.','The dog wandered through the farmyard.','The wanderer crossed the valley.','The first uses wandering to describe a meandering stream.')]);
P('wane','From Old English wanian, “decrease or diminish”; it describes decline, the moon’s decrease in visible area, or the period of decline.',[C('wane.s1','衰减','Public confidence began to wane after officials repeatedly missed their deadlines.','官員屢次錯過期限後，公眾信心開始減弱。','wane / be on the wane','Verb: become gradually weaker, smaller, or less important.' ,'Confidence decreases over time.'),C('wane.s2','月亏','The moon will wane during the two weeks after it reaches its full phase.','月亮到達滿月後的兩週內會逐漸虧缺。','the moon wanes','Verb: become smaller in the visible part of the moon.' ,'The illuminated portion appears to shrink.'),C('wane.s3','衰退期','By the wane of the empire, several provinces had become independent.','帝國走向衰退期時，已有數個行省獨立。','in the wane of + period / power','Noun: a period of decline or weakening.' ,'The noun names the decline phase.')],[M('The moon waned from a thin crescent to a full moon as its visible area steadily increased.','The moon waxed from a thin crescent toward a full moon as its visible area increased.','A waning moon becomes less visible; increasing illumination is waxing.')],[Q('wane.q1','wane.s1','meaning','What happened to public confidence?','It gradually became weaker.','It suddenly became a full moon.','It increased without interruption.','Wane means decrease or decline gradually.'),Q('wane.q2','wane.s2','context','What happens to the visible moon after the full phase?','Its visible illuminated portion gradually shrinks.','It immediately disappears forever.','It moves along a road verge.','The moon wanes as its visible area decreases.'),Q('wane.q3','wane.s3','distinction','What does “the wane of the empire” name?','A period when the empire was declining.','The empire’s strongest period.','A moonlit waiting room.','As a noun, wane is a period of decline.'),Q('wane.q4','wane.s2','word-choice','Choose the lunar use.','The moon wanes during the second half of the cycle.','Interest in the show began to wane.','The empire entered its wane.','The first refers to the shrinking visible moon.')]);
P('wanna','A colloquial pronunciation spelling of want to, formed by reducing and blending the two words in informal speech.',[C('wanna.s1','想要；想做','“You wanna join us for lunch?” Maya asked her colleague.','「你想和我們一起吃午餐嗎？」瑪雅問同事。','wanna + base verb (informal speech)','Colloquial form: want to, used mainly in informal speech or dialogue.' ,'The speaker casually asks whether the colleague wants to join.')],[M('The formal contract used “wanna” as its only standard spelling for want to in a legal clause.','The formal contract used “want to” rather than the conversational spelling “wanna.”','Wanna is informal and is generally avoided in formal writing.')],[Q('wanna.q1','wanna.s1','meaning','What did Maya ask her colleague?','Whether the colleague wanted to join lunch.','Whether the colleague had already eaten yesterday.','Whether the colleague could issue a warrant.','Wanna is an informal form of want to.'),Q('wanna.q2','wanna.s1','context','Where is wanna most natural?','In casual dialogue or a text to a friend.','In a formal legal contract.','In a scientific article’s methods section.','The spelling represents informal spoken reduction.'),Q('wanna.q3','wanna.s1','grammar','What normally follows wanna in “I wanna leave”?','A base-form verb.','A noun with no verb.','A past-tense verb ending in -ed.','Wanna stands for want to, followed by the verb base.'),Q('wanna.q4','wanna.s1','usage','Which sentence is appropriate in formal prose?','I want to discuss the proposal.','I wanna discuss the proposal.','I wanned to discuss the proposal.','Formal prose generally writes want to in full.')]);
P('want','From Old Norse vanta, “be lacking”; meanings include desire, need, absence, and a state of poverty.',[C('want.s1','想要','I want a clear map before we begin the mountain walk.','開始登山前，我想要一張清楚的地圖。','want something / want to do','Verb: wish to have or do something.' ,'The speaker desires a map.'),C('want.s2','需要','The seedlings want more light if they are to grow strong.','幼苗若要茁壯成長，就需要更多光線。','something wants + noun / doing','Verb: need or require something.' ,'The plants require additional light.'),C('want.s3','缺乏','The report was not wanting in detail, but it needed clearer headings.','這份報告並不缺乏細節，但需要更清楚的標題。','be wanting in + quality','Verb: lack or be deficient in something, often formal.' ,'The report has detail and does not lack it.'),C('want.s4','贫困；缺乏','The charity supplied blankets to families living in want during the harsh winter.','嚴冬期間，慈善機構為生活困苦的家庭提供毛毯。','live / be in want','Noun: a state of poverty or lack of necessary things.' ,'The families lack basic resources.')],[M('The report was wanting in detail even though it contained every relevant fact and example.','The report was not wanting in detail because it contained every relevant fact and example.','A report that contains all relevant details does not lack detail.')],[Q('want.q1','want.s1','meaning','What does the speaker desire before the walk?','A clear map.','More sunlight for seedlings.','A state of poverty.','Want as a verb can mean wish to have something.'),Q('want.q2','want.s2','context','What do the seedlings require?','More light to grow well.','A map of the mountain.','A weekly wage.','Want can mean need or require.'),Q('want.q3','want.s3','distinction','What does “not wanting in detail” mean?','It does not lack detail.','It desires more maps.','It lives in poverty.','Wanting in means lacking; not wanting means not lacking.'),Q('want.q4','want.s4','word-choice','Which phrase uses want as a noun?','The families lived in want during the severe winter.','The families want warmer weather.','The report was wanting in detail.','In want names a state of poverty or deprivation.')]);
P('wale','From Old English walu, “ridge or raised mark”; it names a welt or fabric ridge and can mean strike to raise a welt.',[C('wale.s1','隆起伤痕','A narrow wale remained on his arm where the tight strap had pressed the skin.','緊繃的帶子壓過皮膚後，他手臂上留下一道隆起的傷痕。','a raised wale','Noun: a raised mark or welt on the skin.','The strap leaves a raised line.'),C('wale.s2','布面凸条','The corduroy jacket has fine wales running down each sleeve.','這件燈芯絨外套的袖子上有細密的縱向凸條。','wales in cloth','Noun: a raised ridge or stripe in woven fabric.','The fabric has parallel ridges.'),C('wale.s3','抽打','The old story says the guard waled the thief with a leather strap.','舊故事說看守用皮帶抽打了小偷。','wale someone with a strap','Verb: beat so as to raise a welt.','The strap is used to strike the person.')],[M('The corduroy had a smooth, flat surface with no ridges, yet the tailor called each raised stripe a wale.','The corduroy had raised stripes, each of which was a wale.','A cloth wale is a raised ridge, not a flat area.')],[Q('wale.q1','wale.s1','meaning','What remained on his arm?','A raised mark where the strap pressed.','A railway freight car.','A verse from a song.','A skin wale is a raised welt.'),Q('wale.q2','wale.s2','context','What did the tailor notice on the corduroy?','Raised ridges running along the fabric.','A perfectly smooth surface.','A person’s waist measurement.','A cloth wale is a raised stripe.'),Q('wale.q3','wale.s3','distinction','What did the guard do with the strap?','Struck the thief hard enough to raise a welt.','Sewed parallel cloth ridges.','Measured the thief’s sleeve.','Wale as a verb means beat so as to leave a welt.'),Q('wale.q4','wale.s2','word-choice','Choose the fabric use.','The sweater’s knitted wales formed vertical ridges.','The strap left a wale on his skin.','The guard waled the prisoner.','The first describes textile ridges.')]);
P('walk','From Old English wealcan, “roll or toss,” later “move on foot”; it can mean guide someone, a stroll, or a pedestrian path.',[C('walk.s1','步行','We walked through the old market before the shops opened.','商店開門前，我們步行穿過老市場。','walk through / along','Verb: move forward on foot at a regular pace.','They travel by walking.'),C('walk.s2','带着走','She walks her dog beside the canal every morning.','她每天早上沿著運河遛狗。','walk a dog / child home','Verb: take or guide someone on foot.','She accompanies the dog.'),C('walk.s3','散步','We took a short walk after dinner to enjoy the cool air.','晚餐後我們短暫散步，享受涼爽空氣。','take a walk','Noun: a journey or period of walking.','The phrase names an outing on foot.'),C('walk.s4','步道','A wooden walk leads visitors across the marsh.','一條木棧道引領遊客穿過沼澤。','a public walk / boardwalk','Noun: a path intended for people to walk along.','The structure is a pedestrian path.')],[M('They walked across the market by remaining in one place and never moving their feet.','They stayed still in the market instead of walking across it.','Walking requires movement on foot.')],[Q('walk.q1','walk.s1','meaning','How did they cross the market?','They moved through it on foot.','They drove a wagon.','They waited without moving.','Walk as a verb means move on foot.'),Q('walk.q2','walk.s2','context','What does she do with her dog each morning?','Takes it along the canal on foot.','Leaves it alone at home.','Measures its waistline.','Walk an animal means guide it on a walk.'),Q('walk.q3','walk.s3','distinction','What did they take after dinner?','A short stroll.','A jury’s verdict.','A train ticket.','A walk as a noun is a trip on foot.'),Q('walk.q4','walk.s4','word-choice','Which sentence names a path?','The raised walk crosses the marsh.','They walk across the marsh.','They took a walk after lunch.','Here walk is a constructed route.')]);
P('walk out','From walk + out; it means leave a place or stop working as a protest.',[C('walk out.s1','走出；离开','She walked out of the meeting after the chair refused to hear her evidence.','主席拒絕聽取她的證據後，她走出了會議。','walk out of a room / meeting','Phrasal verb: leave a place, often suddenly or in protest.','She exits the meeting.'),C('walk out.s2','罢工','Dockworkers walked out for two days to demand safer equipment.','碼頭工人罷工兩天，要求更安全的設備。','workers walk out; walk out on an employer','Phrasal verb: stop working or withdraw cooperation as protest.','The workers suspend their labor.')],[M('The dockworkers walked out on strike while continuing every shift without interruption.','The dockworkers stayed at work instead of walking out on strike.','A walkout stops work; uninterrupted shifts contradict a strike.')],[Q('walk out.q1','walk out.s1','meaning','What did she do when her evidence was rejected?','She left the meeting.','She served dinner.','She measured a path.','Walk out of a place means leave it.'),Q('walk out.q2','walk out.s2','context','Why did the dockworkers stop work?','To protest and demand safer equipment.','To take a stroll.','To wait for a train.','This sense is a strike or withdrawal of cooperation.'),Q('walk out.q3','walk out.s1','distinction','Which is a literal walkout?','A guest rises and leaves the hall during discussion.','Workers refuse shifts during a labor dispute.','A guard walks a dog.','The first is physically leaving a place.'),Q('walk out.q4','walk out.s2','word-choice','Choose the labor-protest use.','Nurses walked out over unsafe staffing.','She walked out of the cinema after the film.','He walked out to the garden.','The nurses stop work in protest.')]);
P('walker','From walk + -er, a person who walks; it can also mean a race-walking athlete.',[C('walker.s1','步行者','A walker on the coastal path stopped to watch dolphins offshore.','一位沿海步道散步的人停下觀看近海海豚。','a long-distance walker','Noun: a person who travels on foot for exercise or pleasure.','The person is walking for recreation.'),C('walker.s2','竞走运动员','The race walker kept one foot in contact with the track during every stride.','這名競走運動員每一步都讓一隻腳保持接觸跑道。','a competitive walker','Noun: an athlete who competes in race walking.','The athlete follows race-walking technique.')],[M('The walker won the race-walking event while running with both feet off the track.','The runner won by running; a race walker must maintain the required walking action.','Running with both feet airborne violates race-walking technique.')],[Q('walker.q1','walker.s1','meaning','Why did the person stop on the coast path?','To watch dolphins while out on foot.','To serve at a table.','To inspect a freight car.','A walker can be someone walking for pleasure.'),Q('walker.q2','walker.s2','context','What did the athlete maintain during each stride?','At least one foot touched the track.','Both feet were airborne.','The athlete rode in a wagon.','A race walker follows a walking technique.'),Q('walker.q3','walker.s1','distinction','Which person is a recreational walker?','Someone taking a long footpath stroll.','A sprinter in a track race.','A waiter carrying plates.','The first walks for exercise or pleasure.'),Q('walker.q4','walker.s2','word-choice','Choose the sport use.','The Olympic walker trained for a 20-kilometre event.','The walker explored the coastal trail at leisure.','A walker waited at the clinic.','The first names a race-walking athlete.')]);
P('walking','From walk + -ing; it names the activity of going on foot and can describe a route made for pedestrians.',[C('walking.s1','步行；散步','Walking after lunch helps me clear my mind before the afternoon meeting.','午餐後散步有助於我在下午會議前整理思緒。','go / take up walking','Noun: the activity of moving on foot for exercise or travel.','Walking is the activity being discussed.'),C('walking.s2','步行的','They followed a walking route that linked the station to three gardens.','他們沿著一條步行路線，從車站連接到三座花園。','a walking route / holiday','Adjective: involving travel or movement on foot.','The route is designed for people on foot.')],[M('They chose a walking route that could be completed only by driving and never leaving the car.','They chose a driving route that could be completed by car.','A walking route is for travel on foot, not exclusively by car.')],[Q('walking.q1','walking.s1','meaning','What activity helps clear the speaker’s mind?','Moving on foot after lunch.','Driving through the city.','Serving meals.','Walking as a noun names the activity.'),Q('walking.q2','walking.s2','context','How do visitors travel along the garden route?','On foot.','Only by freight train.','By remaining in a car.','The adjective describes a route intended for walking.'),Q('walking.q3','walking.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses walking as a noun?','Walking is part of her daily exercise.','They chose a walking tour.','The walking route starts at the station.','In the first, walking names an activity.'),Q('walking.q4','walking.s2','word-choice','Choose the adjectival use.','A walking map marks paths between villages.','Walking in the hills can be tiring.','She enjoys walking before breakfast.','The first modifies map and describes foot travel.')]);
P('walkout','From walk out, a compound naming a coordinated departure, especially a strike or protest.',[C('walkout.s1','集体离场；罢工','The students staged a walkout to protest the closure of their language program.','學生集體離場，抗議語言課程被關閉。','stage / organize / join a walkout','Noun: a coordinated departure from work or an event, usually in protest.','The students leave together to protest.')],[M('The workers’ walkout consisted of staying at their desks and continuing work without protest.','The workers continued their work at the desks; there was no walkout.','A walkout involves leaving or stopping work, not continuing normally.')],[Q('walkout.q1','walkout.s1','meaning','Why did the students leave together?','To protest the program’s closure.','To take an ordinary stroll.','To enter a waiting room.','A walkout is a coordinated protest departure.'),Q('walkout.q2','walkout.s1','context','Which event is a walkout?','Employees leave the factory floor together during a dispute.','One person walks a dog.','Guests arrive early at a meeting.','The coordinated departure signals protest.'),Q('walkout.q3','walkout.s1','distinction','How does a walkout differ from an ordinary break?','It is organized as a protest or labor action.','It must happen outdoors.','It means a daily walk.','The protest purpose distinguishes a walkout.'),Q('walkout.q4','walkout.s1','word-choice','Choose the protest-noun use.','The nurses’ walkout lasted until talks reopened.','The nurse walked out to answer a call.','The nurse walks her dog after work.','The first names a coordinated labor action.')]);
P('walkway','From walk + way, a passage intended for people travelling on foot.',[C('walkway.s1','走道','A covered walkway connects the library to the science building.','一條有頂走道連接圖書館和科學大樓。','a covered / pedestrian walkway','Noun: a path or passage for people walking.','It lets pedestrians travel between buildings.')],[M('The covered walkway was reserved for cars and had no space for pedestrians.','The covered roadway was reserved for cars and had no pedestrian space.','A walkway is intended for people on foot, not cars only.')],[Q('walkway.q1','walkway.s1','meaning','What does the covered structure connect?','The library and science building.','Two freight wagons.','A courtroom and a restaurant.','A walkway is a passage for pedestrians.'),Q('walkway.q2','walkway.s1','context','Which feature identifies a walkway?','It provides a route for people on foot.','It is reserved for cars only.','It is a room where passengers wait.','The word names a pedestrian path.'),Q('walkway.q3','walkway.s1','distinction','Where would pedestrians use a walkway?','Across a bridge between campus buildings.','Inside a moving freight car.','Around a garment’s waistline.','The bridge passage is built for people walking.'),Q('walkway.q4','walkway.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural use.','A lit walkway runs from the station to the terminal.','The walkway paid each employee a wage.','The walkway returned the jury’s verdict.','A walkway connects pedestrian destinations.')]);
P('wall','From Old English weall, from Latin vallum, “rampart”; it names a structure, a figurative obstacle, or the act of enclosing with walls.',[C('wall.s1','墙壁','A crack appeared in the wall beside the kitchen window.','廚房窗戶旁的牆上出現一道裂縫。','a brick / interior wall','Noun: a vertical structure forming part of a building or room.','The crack is in the building structure.'),C('wall.s2','围墙','A stone wall surrounds the old garden and keeps deer out.','一道石圍牆環繞老花園，阻擋鹿群進入。','a boundary / garden wall','Noun: a structure built around an area for protection or division.','It encloses the garden.'),C('wall.s3','障碍','Lack of funding became a wall between the proposal and its completion.','資金不足成了提案與完成之間的障礙。','a wall between / against progress','Noun: a barrier or obstacle, literal or figurative.','The shortage prevents progress.'),C('wall.s4','用墙围住','They walled the narrow courtyard to keep livestock out.','他們築牆圍住狹窄庭院，以免牲畜進入。','wall off / wall in an area','Verb: enclose or separate a place by building a wall.','The courtyard is enclosed.')],[M('The garden wall protected the plants by leaving the garden completely open to deer.','The garden wall protected the plants by enclosing the garden and keeping deer out.','A boundary wall cannot keep deer out if it leaves the area open.')],[Q('wall.q1','wall.s1','meaning','Where did the crack appear?','In a vertical part of the kitchen structure.','In a weekly paycheck.','In a river’s wake.','Wall can name a building’s vertical structure.'),Q('wall.q2','wall.s2','context','What does the stone wall do?','Encloses the garden and keeps deer out.','Connects buildings as a walkway.','Provides a room for patients.','A boundary wall divides or protects an area.'),Q('wall.q3','wall.s3','distinction','What did lack of funding become?','An obstacle to completing the proposal.','A brick wall in a courtyard.','A garment’s waistline.','The figurative sense is a barrier to progress.'),Q('wall.q4','wall.s4','grammar','What does “They walled off the courtyard” mean?','They enclosed it with a wall.','They covered it with wallpaper.','They walked out of it.','Wall off means enclose or isolate a place.')]);
P('wallet','From Middle English wallet, from Anglo-Norman walet, “small bag”; it means a pocket case or a digital payment account.',[C('wallet.s1','钱包','She put the receipt back in her leather wallet and zipped her bag.','她把收據放回皮夾，然後拉上包包拉鍊。','a leather / billfold wallet','Noun: a small flat case for carrying money, cards, or documents.','The case holds a receipt and small items.'),C('wallet.s2','电子钱包','The customer added a transit pass to the mobile wallet on her phone.','顧客把交通卡加入手機上的電子錢包。','a digital / mobile wallet','Noun: an electronic account or app used to store payment information.','The phone stores payment credentials.')],[M('She paid with her wallet by leaving cash and cards at home and using no digital payment account.','She paid with a mobile wallet that stored her payment information.','A wallet must carry or provide access to payment details.')],[Q('wallet.q1','wallet.s1','meaning','Where did she put the receipt?','In a small case for money and cards.','In a freight wagon.','In a court file.','A wallet is a small case for personal items.'),Q('wallet.q2','wallet.s2','context','What did the customer add to her phone?','A transit pass in a digital payment app.','A paper wall covering.','A garden boundary.','A mobile wallet stores payment information.'),Q('wallet.q3','wallet.s1','distinction','Which wallet is a physical object?','A leather case kept in a jacket pocket.','A payment app on a phone.','A railway carriage.','The leather case is a physical wallet.'),Q('wallet.q4','wallet.s2','word-choice','Choose the digital-payment use.','He tapped the phone’s wallet to pay for the ticket.','He took cash from his pocket wallet.','He left his wallet on the table.','The first refers to an electronic wallet app.')]);
P('wallpaper','From wall + paper, decorative paper fixed to interior walls.',[C('wallpaper.s1','墙纸','They chose pale green wallpaper with a subtle leaf pattern for the bedroom.','他們為臥室挑選淡綠色、帶細緻葉片圖案的壁紙。','hang / remove / patterned wallpaper','Noun: decorative paper fixed to the inside walls of a room.','The paper covers and decorates the walls.')],[M('They decorated the wall with wallpaper by leaving it bare and applying no covering.','They decorated the wall with paint instead of wallpaper.','A bare, uncovered wall has no wallpaper.')],[Q('wallpaper.q1','wallpaper.s1','meaning','What did they choose for the bedroom walls?','Decorative paper with a leaf pattern.','A leather wallet.','A wooden walkway.','Wallpaper is paper used to cover and decorate interior walls.'),Q('wallpaper.q2','wallpaper.s1','context','What would a decorator do with wallpaper?','Paste it onto an interior wall.','Use it to pay for a ticket.','Hang it from a tree as a wage notice.','Wallpaper is fixed to room walls.'),Q('wallpaper.q3','wallpaper.s1','distinction','Which is wallpaper rather than paint?','A patterned sheet covering the wall.','A coloured liquid brushed onto the wall.','A curtain over a window.','Wallpaper is a paper covering.'),Q('wallpaper.q4','wallpaper.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','Strip the old wallpaper before decorating.','Strip the old wallet before decorating.','Strip the old wage before decorating.','Wallpaper is a covering that can be removed from a wall.')]);
P('walnut','From Old English wealhhnutu, “foreign nut,” from wealh, “foreign,” + hnutu, “nut.”',[C('walnut.s1','核桃','Chopped walnut added a rich crunch to the pear salad.','切碎的核桃為梨子沙拉增添了濃郁酥脆的口感。','a walnut kernel / shell','Noun: the edible nut of a walnut tree, usually with a hard wrinkled shell.','The chopped nut adds texture.')],[M('She sprinkled walnut on the salad, describing the ingredient as a leafy herb rather than a nut.','She sprinkled chopped walnut on the salad, using the edible tree nut.','A walnut is a nut, not a leafy herb.')],[Q('walnut.q1','walnut.s1','meaning','What did walnut add to the salad?','A rich crunchy texture.','A paper wall covering.','A metal fastening.','Walnut is an edible nut.'),Q('walnut.q2','walnut.s1','context','What grows on a walnut tree?','Nuts with hard, wrinkled shells.','Small leather wallets.','Railway wagons.','The tree produces walnuts.'),Q('walnut.q3','walnut.s1','distinction','Which ingredient is a walnut?','The edible kernel from a hard-shelled tree nut.','A leafy culinary herb.','A fabric stripe.','Walnut is the nut or edible kernel.'),Q('walnut.q4','walnut.s1','word-choice','Choose the food use.','The baker folded chopped walnuts into the batter.','The baker folded wallpaper into the batter.','The baker folded wages into the batter.','Walnuts are edible nuts used in cooking.')]);
P('walrus','From Dutch walrus, perhaps from a North Germanic source; it names an Arctic marine mammal and informally a thick moustache.',[C('walrus.s1','海象','A walrus hauled itself onto the ice beside a breathing hole.','一頭海象把身體拖上呼吸孔旁的冰面。','an Arctic walrus','Noun: a large Arctic sea mammal with tusks and whiskers.','The animal rests on sea ice.'),C('walrus.s2','海象式胡子','The actor wore a thick walrus that covered his upper lip for the period role.','這名演員為了年代角色留著厚厚的海象式鬍子，遮住上唇。','a walrus moustache','Noun, informal: a thick drooping moustache resembling the animal’s whiskers.','The moustache hangs over the upper lip.')],[M('The Arctic walrus was a small desert insect with no tusks or whiskers.','The Arctic walrus was a large marine mammal with tusks and whiskers.','A walrus is a sea mammal, not a desert insect.')],[Q('walrus.q1','walrus.s1','meaning','What animal climbed onto the ice?','A large Arctic mammal with tusks and whiskers.','A desert insect.','A railway carriage.','A walrus is an Arctic sea mammal.'),Q('walrus.q2','walrus.s2','context','What did the actor wear?','A thick moustache hanging over the upper lip.','A pair of tusks.','A leather waistcoat.','Walrus can informally describe a moustache style.'),Q('walrus.q3','walrus.s1','distinction','Where would a walrus naturally live?','In an Arctic marine environment.','In a hot desert far from water.','In a restaurant waiting room.','Walruses are Arctic marine mammals.'),Q('walrus.q4','walrus.s2','word-choice','Choose the grooming use.','He grew a walrus moustache for the theatre role.','A walrus hauled out on the sea ice.','The walrus dived under Arctic water.','The first describes the moustache style.')]);
P('wan','From Old English wann, “dark, pale, or gloomy”; it describes an unusually pale or sick-looking appearance.',[C('wan.s1','苍白憔悴','After the long fever, he looked wan but was glad to sit up and speak.','長時間發燒後，他看起來蒼白憔悴，但很高興能坐起來說話。','look / grow wan','Adjective: pale and unhealthy-looking, often from illness or tiredness.','His face appears pale after the fever.')],[M('After the fever, he looked wan with a ruddy complexion and vigorous health.','After the fever, he looked healthy with a ruddy complexion.','Wan describes a pale or sickly appearance, not a healthy flush.')],[Q('wan.q1','wan.s1','meaning','How did he look after the fever?','Pale and tired.','Ruddy and full of energy.','Ready to serve a meal.','Wan describes a pale, unhealthy appearance.'),Q('wan.q2','wan.s1','context','Who looks wan?','Someone whose face is pale after a long illness.','Someone with a healthy flushed face after exercise.','Someone standing beside a wall.','Wan suggests pallor or weakness.'),Q('wan.q3','wan.s1','distinction','What contrast best explains wan?','Pale and weary rather than healthy and rosy.','Loud rather than quiet.','Vertical rather than horizontal.','Wan describes a pale, often tired appearance.'),Q('wan.q4','wan.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate sentence.','Her wan face showed how little she had slept.','Her wan face glowed with a deep, healthy tan.','Her wan face was a railway wagon.','The first uses wan for a tired pale appearance.')]);
P('wand','From Old English wand, “rod or slender stick”; it can be a magician’s stick or a thin tool for directing or applying something.',[C('wand.s1','细棒；魔杖','The stage magician tapped the empty box with a silver wand.','舞台魔術師用銀色魔杖敲了敲空盒子。','a magic / conductor’s wand','Noun: a thin stick used by a magician or as a tool for directing or applying something.','The magician holds a slender stick.')],[M('The magician waved a wand, which was a thick stone wall built across the stage.','The magician waved a thin wand across the stage.','A wand is a slender rod, not a wall.')],[Q('wand.q1','wand.s1','meaning','What did the magician tap on the box?','A thin silver rod.','A paper covering.','A garden fence.','A wand is a slender stick or rod.'),Q('wand.q2','wand.s1','context','Which object could be a wand?','A narrow stick used to direct a choir.','A broad brick wall.','A leather wallet.','A wand can direct or apply something.'),Q('wand.q3','wand.s1','distinction','How is a wand different from a wall?','It is a thin handheld stick.','It is a large fixed barrier.','It is a room where people wait.','A wand is a slender rod.'),Q('wand.q4','wand.s1','word-choice','Choose the magical use.','She raised her wand and the stage lights dimmed.','She raised her wallpaper and the lights dimmed.','She raised her wage and the lights dimmed.','A magician raises or waves a wand.')]);
P('wander','From Old English wandrian, “move aimlessly or stray”; it also describes attention straying or a leisurely walk.',[C('wander.s1','漫步','We wandered through the harbor market without choosing a particular route.','我們沒有選定路線，在港口市集裡隨意閒逛。','wander around / through','Verb: walk or travel with no fixed direction or purpose.','They move around without a set route.'),C('wander.s2','偏离；走失','The hikers wandered off the marked trail when fog covered the signs.','霧氣遮住標誌後，健行者偏離了標記步道。','wander off / from a path','Verb: move away from a correct route or subject.','They stray from the trail.'),C('wander.s3','走神','My mind began to wander during the long lecture, and I missed the next instruction.','冗長的演講中，我開始走神，錯過了下一條指示。','mind / attention wanders','Verb: let thoughts drift away from the matter in hand.','Attention shifts away from the lecture.'),C('wander.s4','漫步（名词）','After dinner, we went for a wander along the river.','晚飯後，我們沿著河邊散步。','go for a wander','Noun: a walk or journey without a particular direction.','The phrase names an unplanned stroll.')],[M('The hikers wandered off the trail by following every sign exactly and staying on the marked route.','The hikers stayed on the trail by following the signs exactly.','Wandering off means straying from the marked route.')],[Q('wander.q1','wander.s1','meaning','How did they explore the market?','They walked around without a fixed route.','They followed one marked trail.','They stayed in a waiting room.','Wander can mean move about aimlessly.'),Q('wander.q2','wander.s2','context','Why did the hikers become lost?','They strayed from the marked path in fog.','They stayed on every signposted path.','They explored a harbor market.','Wander off means leave the intended route.'),Q('wander.q3','wander.s3','distinction','What happened during the lecture?','The speaker’s attention drifted from the topic.','The speaker walked off a trail.','The speaker took a river stroll.','A mind can wander when attention strays.'),Q('wander.q4','wander.s4','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','They took a quiet wander along the river.','They wandered around the market.','Their minds wandered during the lecture.','The first uses wander as a noun meaning stroll.')]);
P('wanderer','From wander + -er, a person who travels or roams without a fixed home or route.',[C('wanderer.s1','流浪者','The novel’s wanderer moved from town to town, carrying only a small pack.','小說中的流浪者背著小背包，從一個城鎮走到另一個城鎮。','a solitary / homeless wanderer','Noun: someone who travels from place to place, often without a settled home.','The traveler has no fixed destination.'),C('wanderer.s2','漫游者','The ranger found a wanderer who had left the trail but still had enough water.','巡護員找到一名偏離步道的漫遊者，他的水仍足夠。','a wanderer in the hills / woods','Noun: someone who roams about without a fixed route.','The person is roaming in the area.')],[M('The wanderer never left his fixed home or travelled anywhere else.','The settled resident never left his fixed home or travelled anywhere else.','A wanderer roams or travels rather than remaining in one place.')],[Q('wanderer.q1','wanderer.s1','meaning','How did the novel’s wanderer travel?','From town to town with few possessions.','By staying forever in one house.','By serving meals at a restaurant.','A wanderer may travel without a settled home.'),Q('wanderer.q2','wanderer.s2','context','Why did the ranger find the person?','The person had roamed away from the trail.','The person waited in a clinic.','The person built a wall.','A wanderer can roam without a fixed route.'),Q('wanderer.q3','wanderer.s1','distinction','Which person is a wanderer?','A traveler who moves between places without a settled address.','A person who never leaves one home.','A commuter on the same bus daily.','The first person has no fixed home or route.'),Q('wanderer.q4','wanderer.s2','word-choice','Choose the roaming-person use.','A wanderer explored the forest paths all afternoon.','The wanderer negotiated a weekly wage.','The wanderer served dinner guests.','The first describes someone roaming on foot.')]);
P('wandering','From wander + -ing, describing movement without a fixed route or direction.',[C('wandering.s1','徘徊的；漫游的','A wandering dog appeared at the farm gate after the storm.','暴風雨後，一隻徘徊的狗出現在農場大門口。','a wandering animal / path / gaze','Adjective: moving about without a fixed direction or route.','The dog has no clear route.')],[M('The wandering dog stayed at the same marked spot for years and never moved.','The stationary dog stayed at the same marked spot for years.','Something wandering moves about rather than remaining fixed.')],[Q('wandering.q1','wandering.s1','meaning','What kind of dog appeared at the gate?','One moving about without a fixed route.','One that never moved from a fixed spot.','One trained to serve food.','Wandering describes movement without a set direction.'),Q('wandering.q2','wandering.s1','context','Which gaze is wandering?','Eyes drift from one part of the room to another.','Eyes remain fixed on one point.','Eyes are closed in sleep.','A wandering gaze shifts about.'),Q('wandering.q3','wandering.s1','distinction','What contrasts with a wandering path?','A straight route that stays fixed and direct.','A trail twisting without a set course.','A person roaming between towns.','A fixed direct route is not wandering.'),Q('wandering.q4','wandering.s1','word-choice','Choose the adjectival use.','A wandering stream changed course across the plain.','The dog wandered through the farmyard.','The wanderer crossed the valley.','The first uses wandering to describe a meandering stream.')]);
P('wane','From Old English wanian, “decrease or diminish”; it describes decline, the moon’s shrinking visible area, or a period of decline.',[C('wane.s1','衰减','Public confidence began to wane after officials repeatedly missed deadlines.','官員屢次錯過期限後，公眾信心開始減弱。','wane / be on the wane','Verb: become gradually weaker, smaller, or less important.','Confidence decreases over time.'),C('wane.s2','月亏','The moon will wane during the two weeks after it reaches its full phase.','月亮到達滿月後的兩週內會逐漸虧缺。','the moon wanes','Verb: become smaller in its visible illuminated area.','The visible portion appears to shrink.'),C('wane.s3','衰退期','By the wane of the empire, several provinces had become independent.','帝國走向衰退期時，已有數個行省獨立。','in the wane of + period / power','Noun: a period of decline or weakening.','The noun names the decline phase.')],[M('The moon waned from a thin crescent to a full moon as its visible area steadily increased.','The moon waxed from a thin crescent toward a full moon as its visible area increased.','A waning moon becomes less visible; increasing illumination is waxing.')],[Q('wane.q1','wane.s1','meaning','What happened to public confidence?','It gradually became weaker.','It suddenly became a full moon.','It increased without interruption.','Wane means decline gradually.'),Q('wane.q2','wane.s2','context','What happens after the full moon?','Its visible illuminated portion gradually shrinks.','It disappears forever.','It moves along a road verge.','The moon wanes as its visible area decreases.'),Q('wane.q3','wane.s3','distinction','What does “the wane of the empire” name?','A period when the empire was declining.','The empire’s strongest period.','A moonlit waiting room.','As a noun, wane is a period of decline.'),Q('wane.q4','wane.s2','word-choice','Choose the lunar use.','The moon wanes during the second half of its cycle.','Interest in the show began to wane.','The empire entered its wane.','The first concerns the shrinking visible moon.')]);
P('wanna','A colloquial pronunciation spelling of want to, formed by reducing and blending the words in informal speech.',[C('wanna.s1','想要；想做','“You wanna join us for lunch?” Maya asked her colleague.','「你想和我們一起吃午餐嗎？」瑪雅問同事。','wanna + base verb (informal)','Colloquial form: want to, used mainly in informal speech and dialogue.','The speaker casually asks whether the colleague wants to join.')],[M('The formal contract used “wanna” as its standard spelling for want to in a legal clause.','The formal contract used “want to” rather than the conversational spelling “wanna.”','Wanna is informal and is generally avoided in formal writing.')],[Q('wanna.q1','wanna.s1','meaning','What did Maya ask her colleague?','Whether they wanted to join lunch.','Whether they ate yesterday.','Whether they could issue a warrant.','Wanna is an informal form of want to.'),Q('wanna.q2','wanna.s1','context','Where is wanna most natural?','In casual dialogue or a text to a friend.','In a formal contract.','In a scientific methods section.','The spelling represents informal spoken reduction.'),Q('wanna.q3','wanna.s1','grammar','What follows wanna in “I wanna leave”?','A base-form verb.','A past-tense verb only.','A noun with no verb.','Wanna stands for want to and takes the verb base.'),Q('wanna.q4','wanna.s1','usage','Which is appropriate in formal prose?','I want to discuss the proposal.','I wanna discuss the proposal.','I wanned to discuss the proposal.','Formal prose generally writes want to in full.')]);
P('want','From Old Norse vanta, “be lacking”; meanings include desire, need, absence, and poverty.',[C('want.s1','想要','I want a clear map before we begin the mountain walk.','開始登山前，我想要一張清楚的地圖。','want something / want to do','Verb: wish to have or do something.','The speaker desires a map.'),C('want.s2','需要','The seedlings want more light if they are to grow strong.','幼苗若要茁壯成長，就需要更多光線。','something wants + noun / doing','Verb: need or require something.','The plants require more light.'),C('want.s3','缺乏','The report was not wanting in detail, but it needed clearer headings.','這份報告並不缺乏細節，但需要更清楚的標題。','be wanting in + quality','Verb: lack or be deficient in something, often formal.','The report does not lack detail.'),C('want.s4','贫困；缺乏','The charity supplied blankets to families living in want during the harsh winter.','嚴冬期間，慈善機構為生活困苦的家庭提供毛毯。','live / be in want','Noun: poverty or lack of necessary things.','The families lack basic resources.')],[M('The report was wanting in detail even though it contained every relevant fact and example.','The report was not wanting in detail because it contained every relevant fact and example.','A report containing all relevant details does not lack detail.')],[Q('want.q1','want.s1','meaning','What does the speaker desire before the walk?','A clear map.','More light for seedlings.','A state of poverty.','Want as a verb can mean wish to have.'),Q('want.q2','want.s2','context','What do the seedlings require?','More light to grow well.','A map of the mountain.','A weekly wage.','Want can mean need or require.'),Q('want.q3','want.s3','distinction','What does “not wanting in detail” mean?','It does not lack detail.','It desires more maps.','It lives in poverty.','Wanting in means lacking; not wanting means not lacking.'),Q('want.q4','want.s4','word-choice','Which phrase uses want as a noun?','The families lived in want during the winter.','The families want warmer weather.','The report was wanting in detail.','In want names poverty or deprivation.')]);
P('wanted','From want + -ed; it can describe something desirable, someone sought by police, or a person requested in an advertisement.',[C('wanted.s1','受欢迎；受需要','Skilled translators are wanted by the expanding firm.','成長中的公司需要熟練的譯者。','be wanted by employers','Adjective: desirable and welcome to the people concerned.','The firm hopes to hire the translators.'),C('wanted.s2','被通缉','The wanted suspect was arrested after a witness recognized him at the station.','一名證人在車站認出他後，這名通緝嫌犯被捕。','a wanted suspect','Adjective: being sought by the police as a suspect or offender.','Police are searching for the suspect.'),C('wanted.s3','招聘所需','A help-wanted notice listed the skills required for the seasonal job.','招聘啟事列出了季節性工作的技能要求。','a wanted notice; wanted: cooks','Adjective: looked for or requested, especially in an advertisement.','The notice states whom the employer seeks.')],[M('The wanted suspect meant police had officially cleared him and were no longer looking for him.','The wanted suspect was still being sought by police.','A wanted suspect is sought by law enforcement, not cleared.')],[Q('wanted.q1','wanted.s1','meaning','Why were translators wanted by the firm?','The firm hoped to hire their skills.','Police were searching for them as suspects.','They wrote an advertisement.','This sense means desirable to employers.'),Q('wanted.q2','wanted.s2','context','Why was the suspect called wanted?','Police were looking for him.','A firm had hired him as a translator.','He posted a job advertisement.','A wanted suspect is sought by police.'),Q('wanted.q3','wanted.s3','distinction','What did the help-wanted notice list?','Skills and workers the employer was seeking.','A criminal suspect’s location.','A worker’s hourly pay.','The notice states whom the employer wants to hire.'),Q('wanted.q4','wanted.s1','word-choice','Choose the employer sense.','Experienced nurses are wanted at the new clinic.','The wanted robber was seen near the station.','Two cooks wanted; apply today.','The first says employers need those nurses.')]);
P('war','From Old English wyrre through Old French guerre, “armed conflict”; it also names organized opposition and the act of fighting.',[C('war.s1','战争','The two countries signed a ceasefire after years of war.','兩國經歷多年戰爭後簽署停火協議。','declare / wage / end a war','Noun: armed fighting between countries or large groups.','The countries have fought with armies.'),C('war.s2','对抗行动','The city launched a war on illegal dumping, with fines and neighborhood cleanups.','市政府展開反非法傾倒行動，採取罰款並清理街區。','a war on / against a problem','Noun: a long organized effort to stop something harmful.','The campaign targets a social problem.'),C('war.s3','作战；斗争','The general vowed to war against the invading force until the border was secure.','將軍誓言要與入侵部隊作戰，直到邊境安全為止。','war against / with','Verb: fight a war or struggle hard against someone or something.','The general engages in conflict.')],[M('The countries were at war while both armies laid down their weapons and no fighting took place.','The countries were at peace while both armies laid down their weapons.','War involves fighting; laying down weapons and ending conflict is peace.')],[Q('war.q1','war.s1','meaning','What did the countries end with a ceasefire?','Armed conflict that had lasted for years.','A city cleanup campaign.','A product guarantee.','War can mean armed fighting between countries.'),Q('war.q2','war.s2','context','What did the city’s war on dumping involve?','An organized campaign to stop the practice.','A battle between national armies.','A jury’s verdict.','A war on a problem is a sustained effort.'),Q('war.q3','war.s3','distinction','What did the general vow to do?','Fight against the invading force.','Pay the force weekly wages.','Wait for the force to leave.','The verb war means fight or struggle against.'),Q('war.q4','war.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative campaign sense.','The school began a war against bullying.','The two nations fought a war at the border.','The army warred against the invaders.','The school’s phrase names an organized campaign.')]);
P('warble','From Middle English werble, likely from a Germanic source; it means sing in a quavering trill or a fluttering voice sound.',[C('warble.s1','啭鸣；颤唱','A thrush warbled from the hedge as the first light reached the garden.','第一縷晨光照進花園時，一隻畫眉在樹籬中啭鳴。','birds warble; warble a tune','Verb: sing with a high quivering or trilling sound.','The bird produces a wavering musical song.'),C('warble.s2','颤音','Her voice had a slight warble at the end of each sustained note.','她每次拉長音符時，聲音尾端都帶著些微顫音。','a vocal / musical warble','Noun: a rapid fluttering or quavering movement of the voice.','The sound wavers on each note.')],[M('The bird warbled by producing one flat unchanging tone without a trill or variation.','The bird sang one flat unchanging note instead of warbling.','Warbling involves a quavering or trilling sound.')],[Q('warble.q1','warble.s1','meaning','What did the thrush do in the hedge?','It sang with a high, trilling sound.','It issued a search warrant.','It walked out of the garden.','Warble as a verb means sing in a trill.'),Q('warble.q2','warble.s2','context','What feature did her voice have?','A slight wavering at the end of long notes.','A flat sound with no variation.','A siren’s distant wail.','A warble as a noun is a quavering vocal sound.'),Q('warble.q3','warble.s1','distinction','Which bird is warbling?','One singing a sequence of high rippling notes.','One remaining silent on a branch.','One carrying goods in a wagon.','The first sings with a trill.'),Q('warble.q4','warble.s2','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','A soft warble marked the singer’s final note.','The singer warbled the melody softly.','The bird warbled from the hedge.','The first uses warble to name a sound.')]);
P('warbler','From warble + -er; it names a small trilling songbird and can also refer to a singer.',[C('warbler.s1','莺类；歌者','A small warbler searched the willow leaves for insects while singing.','一隻小型鶯類一邊歌唱，一邊在柳葉間尋找昆蟲。','a willow / garden warbler','Noun: a small bird known for its trilling song; also, a singer.','The bird sings as it forages.')],[M('The field guide identified the silent walrus as a warbler, a small songbird with a trilling call.','The field guide identified the small trilling songbird as a warbler.','A walrus is a marine mammal, not a small songbird.')],[Q('warbler.q1','warbler.s1','meaning','What searched among the willow leaves?','A small songbird.','A marine mammal with tusks.','A restaurant server.','A warbler is a small bird known for its song.'),Q('warbler.q2','warbler.s1','context','What was the warbler doing as it searched for insects?','Singing among the leaves.','Building a railway wagon.','Measuring a garment.','Warblers are known for trilling songs.'),Q('warbler.q3','warbler.s1','distinction','Which description fits a warbler?','A small bird that sings a trill.','A large Arctic animal with tusks.','A person waiting for a train.','The source sense is a small songbird.'),Q('warbler.q4','warbler.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural use.','A warbler’s song came from the willow thicket.','A warbler’s wages arrived on Friday.','The warbler issued a court warrant.','The first describes the bird singing.')]);
P('ward','From Old English weard, “guard”; it can mean a hospital unit, someone under guardianship, a city district, or protection against danger.',[C('ward.s1','病房','A nurse moved the patient to a quieter ward after the procedure.','手術後，護士把病人轉到較安靜的病房。','a hospital / maternity ward','Noun: a hospital section for patients needing similar care.','The patient moves to a hospital unit.'),C('ward.s2','受监护人','The court appointed an aunt as guardian of the child, who became her ward.','法院指定姑媽為孩子的監護人，孩子因此成為她的受監護人。','a ward of the court / guardian','Noun: a person under the legal care of a guardian or court.','The child is legally cared for by the aunt.'),C('ward.s3','选区','Each ward elects one representative to the city council.','每個選區選出一名市議會代表。','a city / electoral ward','Noun: an area of a city used for local government or elections.','The district chooses a council member.'),C('ward.s4','挡开；防止','The thick gloves helped ward off the cold during the night patrol.','厚手套幫助巡夜人抵禦夜間寒冷。','ward off + danger / attack / illness','Verb: prevent something dangerous or unwanted from affecting you.','The gloves protect against cold.')],[M('The gloves warded off the cold by leaving his hands exposed to freezing air.','The gloves failed to ward off the cold because his hands were left exposed.','To ward off cold means protect against it.')],[Q('ward.q1','ward.s1','meaning','Where did the nurse move the patient?','To a hospital section for care.','To an electoral district.','To a costume department.','Ward can mean a hospital unit.'),Q('ward.q2','ward.s2','context','What is the child’s legal status?','Under the aunt’s guardianship.','A city council district.','A hospital building.','A ward is someone under legal care.'),Q('ward.q3','ward.s3','distinction','What does each ward elect?','A representative to the city council.','A hospital patient.','A prison warden.','A city ward is a local government district.'),Q('ward.q4','ward.s4','word-choice','Choose the verb meaning “protect against.”','A scarf helped ward off the wind.','The patient stayed in the north ward.','The child was a ward of the court.','Ward off means keep danger or discomfort away.')]);
P('warden','From ward + -en, via Anglo-French wardein; it means a person entrusted with guarding or supervising a place.',[C('warden.s1','监管人','The prison warden inspected the cell block before the evening count.','監獄管理員在晚間點名前檢查牢房區。','prison / park / hostel warden','Noun: a person in charge of a facility or enforcement of rules.','The official supervises the prison.')],[M('The prison warden was responsible for the facility but had no duties or authority over it.','The prison warden supervised the facility and its staff.','A warden is a person in charge of or supervising a place.')],[Q('warden.q1','warden.s1','meaning','What did the prison warden inspect?','The cell block before the evening count.','A restaurant menu.','A river’s wake.','A warden supervises a prison or similar facility.'),Q('warden.q2','warden.s1','context','Who might enforce rules in a national park?','A park warden.','A hospital patient’s ward.','A race walker.','A warden may supervise a park and its regulations.'),Q('warden.q3','warden.s1','distinction','What role does a hostel warden have?','Supervising the hostel and its rules.','Waiting to be served at a table.','Measuring a guest’s waist.','A warden is in charge of a facility.'),Q('warden.q4','warden.s1','word-choice','Choose the supervisory use.','The warden checked that visitors followed reserve rules.','The ward held patients after surgery.','A warning sign marked the trail.','The first names a person enforcing regulations.')]);
P('wardrobe','From Old French garderobe, “place for keeping clothes,” from garder, “guard,” + robe, “clothing.”',[C('wardrobe.s1','衣柜','She hung the winter coats in the tall wardrobe beside the bedroom door.','她把冬季外套掛進臥室門旁的高衣櫃。','a built-in / wooden wardrobe','Noun: a tall cupboard where clothes are stored.','The coats are hung in a storage cabinet.'),C('wardrobe.s2','全部服装','The actor’s wardrobe for the historical series included uniforms and gowns.','這位演員出演歷史劇時的全部服裝包括制服和長袍。','a summer / work / personal wardrobe','Noun: all the clothes a person owns or wears for a purpose.','The word refers to a collection of outfits.'),C('wardrobe.s3','戏装部','The wardrobe department repaired a torn costume before the evening performance.','服裝部在晚間演出前修補了一件破損戲服。','the wardrobe department; stage wardrobe','Noun: costumes for a play or the department responsible for them.','The staff maintain production costumes.')],[M('The actor’s wardrobe for the series contained no clothes or costumes of any kind.','The actor’s wardrobe for the series contained uniforms, gowns, and costumes.','A wardrobe can mean a collection of clothes or costumes.')],[Q('wardrobe.q1','wardrobe.s1','meaning','Where did she hang the winter coats?','In a tall clothes cupboard.','In a hospital ward.','On a railway wagon.','Wardrobe can mean a cabinet for storing clothes.'),Q('wardrobe.q2','wardrobe.s2','context','What did the actor’s wardrobe include?','The collection of clothes worn for the series.','Only the bedroom cupboard.','A warden’s rules.','The person sense refers to all their clothes.'),Q('wardrobe.q3','wardrobe.s3','distinction','What did the wardrobe department repair?','A costume for the performance.','A wooden clothes cupboard.','A council district.','The theatrical sense names costumes or their department.'),Q('wardrobe.q4','wardrobe.s1','word-choice','Choose the furniture use.','She put her coats inside a wardrobe.','The actor’s wardrobe changed between scenes.','The wardrobe department altered a costume.','The first refers to the storage cabinet.')]);
P('ware','From Old English waru, “goods or merchandise”; in compounds, it names objects made of a material or intended for a use.',[C('ware.s1','商品','The market stalls displayed handmade wares from villages along the coast.','市集攤位展示沿海村莊製作的手工商品。','sell / display / household wares','Noun, usually plural: articles offered for sale.','The stalls offer goods to customers.'),C('ware.s2','器皿；制品','The museum labels the blue bowls as stoneware because they are made from fired clay.','博物館把藍色碗標為炻器，因為它們由燒製黏土製成。','stoneware / glassware / tableware','Noun in compounds: objects made of a stated material or for a stated use.','The compound identifies a ceramic ware.')],[M('The market sold handmade wares, meaning the empty stalls and no goods offered to buyers.','The market displayed handmade wares for buyers to purchase.','Wares are articles for sale, not empty stalls.')],[Q('ware.q1','ware.s1','meaning','What did the market stalls display?','Goods made by coastal villagers.','A row of empty stalls.','A hospital ward.','Wares are articles offered for sale.'),Q('ware.q2','ware.s2','context','What does stoneware identify?','Objects made from fired clay.','A prison supervisor.','A clothing collection.','The compound names objects made of a material.'),Q('ware.q3','ware.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses ware as merchandise?','The shop arranged its wares in the front window.','The potter fired stoneware in a kiln.','The glassware broke in shipping.','The first uses wares to mean goods for sale.'),Q('ware.q4','ware.s2','word-choice','Choose the compound-material use.','The cabinet held delicate glassware.','The market sold household wares.','The shop displayed its wares.','Glassware names objects made of glass.')]);
P('warehouse','From ware + house, a building for storing goods before sale or shipment; it is also a verb.',[C('warehouse.s1','仓库','The company stored spare parts in a warehouse near the port.','公司把備用零件存放在港口附近的倉庫裡。','a distribution / storage warehouse','Noun: a large building where goods are kept before being sold or moved.','The parts are held in a storage building.'),C('warehouse.s2','存入仓库','The exporter warehoused the grain until shipping prices fell.','出口商把穀物存入倉庫，直到運費下降。','warehouse goods / stock','Verb: put goods into a warehouse and keep them there.','The exporter stores the grain temporarily.')],[M('The exporter warehoused the grain by selling it immediately and keeping none in storage.','The exporter shipped the grain immediately instead of warehousing it.','To warehouse goods means keep them in a warehouse.')],[Q('warehouse.q1','warehouse.s1','meaning','Where did the company keep spare parts?','In a large storage building near the port.','In a passenger waiting room.','In a coat cupboard.','A warehouse is a building for storing goods.'),Q('warehouse.q2','warehouse.s2','context','Why did the exporter warehouse grain?','To store it until shipping prices fell.','To sell every grain immediately.','To turn it into wallpaper.','As a verb, warehouse means put goods in storage.'),Q('warehouse.q3','warehouse.s1','distinction','Which place is a warehouse?','A building holding stock before distribution.','A hospital section for patients.','A covered pedestrian passage.','The building stores goods before they move onward.'),Q('warehouse.q4','warehouse.s2','grammar','Which sentence uses warehouse as a verb?','They warehoused the furniture during the renovation.','The furniture sat inside a warehouse.','The warehouse stood by the port.','The first uses warehoused as an action.')]);
P('warfare','From war + fare, “course of action”; it means armed fighting or a particular method of competing or attacking.',[C('warfare.s1','作战','The report describes naval warfare in the northern sea during the conflict.','報告描述了衝突期間北方海域的海戰。','naval / aerial / guerrilla warfare','Noun: the activity of fighting in a war.','The report concerns military fighting.'),C('warfare.s2','斗争方式','The campaign became a form of economic warfare, using sanctions rather than weapons.','這場行動成為經濟戰，以制裁而非武器進行鬥爭。','economic / psychological / cyber warfare','Noun: a method of competing or attacking.','The parties use a nonmilitary method.')],[M('The report called a peaceful exchange of gifts naval warfare although no fighting or attack took place.','The report described the armed conflict at sea as naval warfare.','Warfare involves fighting or a method of attack, not a peaceful gift exchange.')],[Q('warfare.q1','warfare.s1','meaning','What does the report describe?','Military fighting at sea.','A peaceful exchange of gifts.','A person’s wardrobe.','Warfare can mean fighting in a war.'),Q('warfare.q2','warfare.s2','context','How did the campaign conduct economic warfare?','By using sanctions instead of weapons.','By storing grain in a warehouse.','By fighting with ships at sea.','This sense is a method of competing or attacking.'),Q('warfare.q3','warfare.s1','distinction','Which phrase describes armed conflict?','aerial warfare','a waiting room','a waistline','Aerial warfare is fighting carried out from aircraft.'),Q('warfare.q4','warfare.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative-method sense.','The firms used price warfare to win customers.','The armies fought naval warfare.','The report covered wartime battles.','The first uses warfare as a competitive tactic.')]);
P('warm','From Old English wearm; it describes moderate heat, friendly feeling, the act of heating, and a warm place.',[C('warm.s1','温暖的','A warm breeze came through the open window on the spring afternoon.','春日下午，一陣暖風從敞開的窗戶吹進來。','warm weather / water / clothes','Adjective: fairly high in temperature, between cool and hot.','The breeze feels comfortably hot.'),C('warm.s2','热情的','The host gave us a warm welcome and introduced everyone by name.','主人熱情地迎接我們，並逐一介紹大家。','a warm welcome / smile','Adjective: friendly, kind, and showing lively feeling.','The host behaves in a friendly way.'),C('warm.s3','使变暖','Warm the milk gently before adding it to the mixture.','把牛奶稍微加熱後再倒入混合物。','warm something; warm up','Verb: make something warm or become warm.','The milk’s temperature is raised.'),C('warm.s4','暖和处','The cat found a warm by the stove and curled up there.','貓在火爐旁找到一處暖和的地方，蜷縮在那裡。','sit in the warm','Noun: a warm place or state of being warm.','The cat settles in a heated spot.')],[M('The host gave visitors a warm welcome by greeting them with hostility and refusing to speak.','The host gave visitors a cold reception by greeting them with hostility.','Warm in a social sense means friendly, not hostile.')],[Q('warm.q1','warm.s1','meaning','How did the spring breeze feel?','Fairly hot but not extremely hot.','Freezing and icy.','Friendly as a person.','Warm as an adjective describes moderate heat.'),Q('warm.q2','warm.s2','context','What kind of welcome did the host give?','A friendly and kind greeting.','A high temperature for milk.','A room for hospital patients.','Warm can describe friendly feelings or behavior.'),Q('warm.q3','warm.s3','distinction','What should happen to the milk?','Its temperature should rise gently.','It should freeze solid.','It should be left untouched.','Warm as a verb means make or become warm.'),Q('warm.q4','warm.s4','word-choice','Choose the noun use.','They sat in the warm beside the stove.','They warmed soup on the stove.','They received a warm welcome.','The first uses warm to mean a warm place or state.')]);
P('warming','From warm + -ing; it names raising temperature and, in climate science, long-term global temperature rise.',[C('warming.s1','加热；升温','The slow warming of the soup took ten minutes over low heat.','用小火慢慢把湯加熱花了十分鐘。','gradual / rapid warming','Noun: the process of raising a thing’s or place’s temperature.','The soup becomes hotter.'),C('warming.s2','全球变暖','The report links global warming to a long-term rise in Earth’s average temperature.','報告將全球暖化與地球平均氣溫長期上升聯繫起來。','global warming','Noun: the long-term increase in the planet’s average temperature.','The topic is climate-scale change.')],[M('The report defined global warming as a long-term fall in Earth’s average temperature.','The report defined global cooling as a long-term fall in Earth’s average temperature.','Warming means a rise in temperature, not a fall.')],[Q('warming.q1','warming.s1','meaning','What happened to the soup?','Its temperature rose gradually.','It cooled to freezing.','It was put in storage.','Warming is a process that raises temperature.'),Q('warming.q2','warming.s2','context','What trend did the climate report describe?','A long-term rise in Earth’s average temperature.','A brief change in one kitchen pot.','A fall in the planet’s average temperature.','Global warming names a planetary temperature increase.'),Q('warming.q3','warming.s1','distinction','Which is an example of warming?','A metal bar grows hotter in a furnace.','Ice melts into colder water.','A room loses heat overnight.','The bar’s temperature rises.'),Q('warming.q4','warming.s2','word-choice','Choose the climate-science use.','Researchers studied the effects of global warming.','The cook monitored the soup’s warming.','The heater began warming the room.','The first refers to long-term climate change.')]);
P('warmth','From warm + -th; it names physical heat or friendly affection.',[C('warmth.s1','温暖；热度','The blanket retained enough warmth to keep the child comfortable overnight.','毯子保留了足夠的熱度，讓孩子整夜都感到舒適。','retain / feel / give warmth','Noun: heat felt near a fire, in a warm room, or from a body.','The blanket keeps the child warm.'),C('warmth.s2','温情','She thanked the volunteers with genuine warmth after the long day.','漫長的一天結束後，她真誠而溫暖地向志工致謝。','speak / greet someone with warmth','Noun: kindness and affectionate feeling shown to another person.','Her thanks convey kindness.')],[M('She thanked the volunteers with warmth by treating them coldly and showing no affection.','She thanked the volunteers coldly, without showing warmth.','Warmth in this sense means kindness, not coldness.')],[Q('warmth.q1','warmth.s1','meaning','What did the blanket retain?','Heat that kept the child comfortable.','The volunteers’ gratitude.','A legal guarantee.','Warmth can mean physical heat.'),Q('warmth.q2','warmth.s2','context','How did she thank the volunteers?','With kindness and affection.','With hostility and silence.','With a higher wage.','Warmth can describe emotional kindness.'),Q('warmth.q3','warmth.s1','distinction','Which use is about physical heat?','The fire gave warmth to the room.','Her warmth welcomed newcomers.','He spoke warmly about friends.','The first refers to heat from a fire.'),Q('warmth.q4','warmth.s2','word-choice','Choose the affectionate sense.','The teacher greeted each new student with warmth.','The blanket trapped warmth around the child.','The sun added warmth to the courtyard.','The greeting shows friendliness and care.')]);
P('warn','From Old English warnian, “give notice or caution”; it can alert someone to danger, advise against an action, or give advance notice.',[C('warn.s1','警告危险','The lifeguard warned swimmers that a strong current was pulling toward the rocks.','救生員警告泳客，強勁水流正把人拉向礁石。','warn someone of / about danger','Verb: tell someone that danger or something unpleasant may happen.','The lifeguard alerts them to a risk.'),C('warn.s2','告诫不要做','The doctor warned him not to stop the medicine without medical advice.','醫生告誡他不要在沒有醫療建議下停藥。','warn someone not to do something','Verb: advise someone strongly against an action.','The doctor discourages a specific action.'),C('warn.s3','预先通知','The landlord warned tenants in advance that water service would be interrupted.','房東提前通知租戶供水服務將暫停。','warn someone in advance','Verb: tell someone beforehand about a possible problem or event.','The notice comes before the interruption.')],[M('The lifeguard warned swimmers of the current by assuring them that the water was perfectly safe.','The lifeguard warned swimmers that the current could pull them toward the rocks.','A warning alerts people to danger; claiming there is none contradicts it.')],[Q('warn.q1','warn.s1','meaning','What did the lifeguard tell swimmers?','A strong current could pull them toward rocks.','Their medicine should be stopped.','Water service would be cut next week.','Warn can alert someone to danger.'),Q('warn.q2','warn.s2','context','What did the doctor advise against?','Stopping the medicine without medical advice.','Swimming near the rocks.','Entering a hospital ward.','Warn someone not to do something is strong advice.'),Q('warn.q3','warn.s3','distinction','When did tenants hear about the water interruption?','Before it happened.','After service returned.','Only during the repair.','Warn in advance means give prior notice.'),Q('warn.q4','warn.s1','grammar','Which construction introduces the danger?','warn someone of a current','warn someone a current to','warn someone by a current of','Warn someone of something is a standard pattern.')]);
P('warning','From warn + -ing; it can be a caution, a danger sign, a lesson from a past mistake, or an ominous indication.',[C('warning.s1','警告','The guide gave a warning about loose stones before the group began climbing.','團體開始攀登前，導遊提醒大家注意鬆動的石塊。','give / issue / heed a warning','Noun: a statement alerting someone to danger or something to avoid.','The guide names a risk.'),C('warning.s2','警示标志','A yellow warning on the gate told visitors to keep clear of the machinery.','大門上的黃色警示標誌告訴訪客要遠離機械。','a warning sign / label','Noun: a sign or notice marking a danger or rule.','The sign gives a visual caution.'),C('warning.s3','前车之鉴','The failed bridge project was a warning against ignoring soil surveys.','橋梁工程失敗是個前車之鑑，提醒人們不要忽視土壤調查。','a warning against + action','Noun: an example showing the consequences of a mistake.','The failure serves as a lesson.'),C('warning.s4','不祥征兆','The sudden pressure drop was a warning that the storm was approaching.','氣壓突然下降是不祥徵兆，預示風暴即將來臨。','a warning of / that + event','Noun: a sign that something bad is likely to happen.','The pressure change signals danger.')],[M('The warning sign told visitors to approach the moving machinery and ignore every safety rule.','The warning sign told visitors to keep clear of the moving machinery.','A warning sign alerts people to danger, not toward it.')],[Q('warning.q1','warning.s1','meaning','What did the guide warn the climbers about?','Loose stones on the route.','A rise in warm weather.','A theatre costume department.','A warning statement alerts people to danger.'),Q('warning.q2','warning.s2','context','What did the yellow notice do?','Marked danger and told visitors to keep clear.','Recorded a jury’s verdict.','Advertised a job opening.','A warning sign gives a visual caution.'),Q('warning.q3','warning.s3','distinction','What lesson did the failed bridge project teach?','Do not ignore soil surveys.','Build without inspecting the site.','Wait in the hospital ward.','A past failure can serve as a warning lesson.'),Q('warning.q4','warning.s4','word-choice','Which is a warning sign of a storm?','A sudden drop in air pressure.','A coat hanging in a wardrobe.','A worker’s wages.','The pressure change signals likely bad weather.')]);
P('warp','From Old English weorpan, “throw or cast”; the modern verb means twist a material or judgment out of shape.',[C('warp.s1','弄弯；曲解','Heat from the radiator warped the wooden shelf, so it no longer sat flat.','暖氣片散出的熱使木架變形，因此它不再平整。','warp wood / plastic; warp judgment','Verb: twist a material out of shape or distort judgment.','The shelf bends because of heat.')],[M('The heat warped the shelf by keeping the wood perfectly flat and unchanged.','The heat left the shelf unchanged; it did not warp the wood.','Warp means distort or bend from the proper shape.')],[Q('warp.q1','warp.s1','meaning','What did radiator heat do to the shelf?','Bent it out of its flat shape.','Turned it into a hospital ward.','Raised its weekly wage.','Warp means twist something out of shape.'),Q('warp.q2','warp.s1','context','What might sunlight do to a plastic panel?','Warp it until it bends.','Give it a warranty.','Make it wait for a train.','Heat can distort the panel’s shape.'),Q('warp.q3','warp.s1','distinction','What does “fear warped his judgment” mean?','Fear distorted how he judged the situation.','Fear made him taller.','Fear improved his reasoning without affecting it.','The figurative sense is distortion of judgment.'),Q('warp.q4','warp.s1','word-choice','Choose the physical-shape use.','Moisture warped the door so it would not close.','Bias warped the judge’s view.','The story warped public opinion.','The first describes physical bending.')]);
P('warrant','From Anglo-French warant, “protection or guarantee,” from a Germanic source; it can mean an official document, justification, justifying action, or a formal promise.',[C('warrant.s1','令状','Officers showed a search warrant before entering the apartment.','警員進入公寓前出示了搜查令。','issue / execute / obtain a warrant','Noun: an official document authorizing arrest or a search.','The document gives legal authority.'),C('warrant.s2','正当理由','There was no warrant for delaying evacuation once smoke entered the stairwell.','煙霧進入樓梯間後，沒有正當理由可以拖延疏散。','no warrant for an action','Noun: a good reason that makes an action acceptable.','The sentence says no justification exists.'),C('warrant.s3','证明正当；需要','The evidence does not warrant a conclusion that the driver acted deliberately.','證據不足以證明司機是故意行事。','evidence warrants a conclusion','Verb: be a good enough reason for something or make it necessary.','The evidence does not justify that conclusion.'),C('warrant.s4','正式保证','The maker warrants that the battery will retain its charge for two years.','製造商保證電池兩年內能維持電量。','warrant that; warrant a product','Verb: promise formally that something is true or will work.','The maker gives a formal assurance.')],[M('The officers searched the apartment without a warrant, although they had shown an official search document first.','The officers searched the apartment under the warrant they had obtained.','Showing an official search warrant means they had legal authorization.')],[Q('warrant.q1','warrant.s1','meaning','What did the officers show before searching?','An official document authorizing the search.','A restaurant menu.','A product warranty.','A warrant is a legal document allowing a search or arrest.'),Q('warrant.q2','warrant.s2','context','Was there a good reason to delay evacuation?','No; smoke in the stairwell left no justification for delay.','Yes; smoke made evacuation unnecessary.','The reason was a product guarantee.','Warrant as a noun can mean justification.'),Q('warrant.q3','warrant.s3','distinction','What does “the evidence does not warrant that conclusion” mean?','The evidence is insufficient to justify it.','The evidence is a search document.','The evidence guarantees the conclusion.','Warrant as a verb can mean justify.'),Q('warrant.q4','warrant.s4','word-choice','Choose the formal-promise use.','The seller warrants that the device meets its specifications.','The judge issued a warrant to search the shop.','The evidence warrants a closer look.','The seller formally guarantees the device.')]);
P('warrantable','From warrant + -able; it describes something capable of justification or eligible for warranty coverage.',[C('warrantable.s1','有正当理由；可保修','The repair was warrantable because the fault appeared within the seller’s two-year guarantee.','故障在賣方兩年保固期內出現，因此這項維修符合保固條件。','a warrantable claim / repair','Adjective: capable of being justified or covered by a warranty.','The claim falls within the guarantee terms.')],[M('The repair was warrantable even though the guarantee had expired and the damage came from deliberate misuse.','The repair was not warrantable because the guarantee had expired and misuse caused the damage.','An expired guarantee and excluded misuse do not support coverage.')],[Q('warrantable.q1','warrantable.s1','meaning','Why was the repair warrantable?','The fault appeared while the guarantee was valid.','The warranty had expired years before.','The damage was deliberately caused by misuse.','Warrantable can mean eligible for warranty coverage.'),Q('warrantable.q2','warrantable.s1','context','Which expense is warrantable?','A repair covered by the written guarantee.','A personal purchase unrelated to the product.','A repair explicitly excluded by the terms.','The guarantee makes the repair eligible.'),Q('warrantable.q3','warrantable.s1','distinction','What can warrantable also mean in an argument?','Capable of being justified by good reasons.','Already proved false.','An official search document.','The adjective can mean defensible or justified.'),Q('warrantable.q4','warrantable.s1','word-choice','Choose the warranty-coverage use.','The manufacturer accepted the warrantable battery claim.','The manufacturer rejected a claim with no warranty.','The judge issued a search warrant.','The first says the claim qualifies for coverage.')]);
P('warranty','From warrant + -y, via Anglo-French warantie, “guarantee”; it means a seller’s repair promise or a contractual assurance.',[C('warranty.s1','保修承诺','The laptop’s warranty covers parts and labor for two years after purchase.','這台筆電的保固涵蓋購買後兩年的零件和人工。','a two-year warranty; warranty covers','Noun: a seller’s written promise to repair or replace goods within a set period.','The product is covered for a stated time.'),C('warranty.s2','合同保证','The contract includes a warranty that all safety reports are complete and accurate.','合約保證所有安全報告均完整且準確。','a warranty that + clause','Noun: a formal promise in a contract that something is true or will be done.','The contract formally assures the reports’ accuracy.')],[M('The laptop warranty promised free repair for two years, but the sentence says it made no promise about repair or replacement.','The laptop warranty promised repair or replacement within the stated period.','A warranty is a promise about covered repair, replacement, or performance.')],[Q('warranty.q1','warranty.s1','meaning','What does the laptop warranty cover?','Parts and labor for two years.','The owner’s weekly wages.','A search of the laptop.','A product warranty promises repair or replacement for a period.'),Q('warranty.q2','warranty.s2','context','What does the contract warranty assure?','That the safety reports are complete and accurate.','That the laptop is a court document.','That the reports have no authors.','A contractual warranty is a formal assurance.'),Q('warranty.q3','warranty.s1','distinction','Which document would contain a product warranty?','A booklet explaining covered repairs after purchase.','A notice listing a suspect wanted by police.','A map of an electoral ward.','The booklet sets out the seller’s product promise.'),Q('warranty.q4','warranty.s2','word-choice','Choose the contractual-assurance use.','The supplier gave a warranty that the data were accurate.','The seller repaired the laptop under warranty.','The customer claimed replacement under warranty.','The first is a formal promise in a contract.')]);
P('warren','From Anglo-Norman warenne, an enclosure for game; it names connected rabbit burrows and can describe a maze-like complex.',[C('warren.s1','兔穴群','At dusk, rabbits disappeared into the warren beneath the sandy bank.','黃昏時，兔子消失在沙坡下的兔穴群中。','a rabbit warren','Noun: an area of connected burrows where rabbits live and breed; also a maze-like building or district.','The rabbits enter a network of burrows.')],[M('The rabbits lived in a warren made of one isolated burrow with no tunnels or connected passages.','The rabbits lived in a single burrow rather than a warren of connected tunnels.','A warren is a connected area of burrows, not one isolated hole.')],[Q('warren.q1','warren.s1','meaning','Where did the rabbits disappear?','Into connected burrows beneath the bank.','Into a hospital ward.','Into a train carriage.','A warren is an area of linked rabbit burrows.'),Q('warren.q2','warren.s1','context','What might “a warren of narrow lanes” describe?','A confusing network of crowded passages.','A single straight road with no side streets.','A grain storage building.','Warren can figuratively mean a maze-like district.'),Q('warren.q3','warren.s1','distinction','Which place is a rabbit warren?','A hillside with many linked rabbit tunnels.','One isolated hole with no passages.','A clothes cupboard in a bedroom.','A warren contains connected burrows.'),Q('warren.q4','warren.s1','word-choice','Choose the literal animal-home use.','The rabbits raised their young in a warren under the bank.','The old quarter was a warren of alleys.','The office was a warren of corridors.','The first names the rabbits’ burrow system.')]);
P('warrior','From Old North French werreier, “make war,” related to war; it can name a fighter or a person who energetically serves a cause.',[C('warrior.s1','战士','The warrior carried a shield into battle and defended the mountain pass.','這名戰士帶著盾牌上戰場，守衛山口。','a brave / skilled warrior','Noun: a person experienced in fighting, especially in older times.','The person is trained for combat.'),C('warrior.s2','斗士','She became a tireless warrior for clean water in rural communities.','她成了為鄉村社區爭取潔淨水源的不懈鬥士。','a warrior for / against a cause','Noun: a person who works energetically for a belief or cause.','She devotes effort to a campaign.')],[M('The warrior for clean water opposed the cause, refused all work, and did nothing to support it.','The opponent of clean-water access refused to support the cause.','A warrior for a cause actively works to advance it.')],[Q('warrior.q1','warrior.s1','meaning','What did the warrior defend?','A mountain pass during battle.','A company’s warranty.','A waiting room.','This sense is a person experienced in fighting.'),Q('warrior.q2','warrior.s2','context','What cause did she champion?','Access to clean water in rural communities.','A military attack on a pass.','A longer wait at the clinic.','A warrior can figuratively work hard for a cause.'),Q('warrior.q3','warrior.s1','distinction','Which person is a literal warrior in the historical sense?','A trained fighter carrying a shield into battle.','An advocate organizing a water campaign.','A night watchman at a gate.','The first is experienced in armed fighting.'),Q('warrior.q4','warrior.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative advocacy use.','He was a warrior for equal access to education.','The warrior defended the castle in battle.','A warrior carried a sword into the field.','The first describes energetic work for a belief.')]);
P('wartime','From war + time; it means the period while a war is taking place.',[C('wartime.s1','战争时期','The factory switched to making medical supplies during wartime.','戰爭期間，工廠改為生產醫療用品。','during / in wartime','Noun: the time during which a war is going on.','The production change occurs while war is active.')],[M('The memoir describes wartime as the peaceful decade after all wars had ended.','The memoir describes peacetime as the peaceful period after the wars ended.','Wartime is a period when a war is in progress, not after it ends.')],[Q('wartime.q1','wartime.s1','meaning','When did the factory make medical supplies?','While a war was taking place.','During a peaceful decade after all wars ended.','Only on weekends.','Wartime is the period during a war.'),Q('wartime.q2','wartime.s1','context','Which scene is set in wartime?','A city rations fuel while its country is at war.','A country celebrates years after a peace treaty.','A factory closes for a summer holiday.','Rationing occurs during the active conflict.'),Q('wartime.q3','wartime.s1','distinction','What contrasts with wartime?','Peacetime','Night watch','A wedding reception','Peacetime is when no war is being fought.'),Q('wartime.q4','wartime.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct phrase.','The bridge was rebuilt in the years after wartime.','The bridge was rebuilt during wartime after the war ended.','The bridge was rebuilt in a wartime that had no conflict.','The first uses wartime for the period of conflict.')]);
P('wary','From Old English wær, “cautious or aware”; it describes carefulness about danger and watchful alertness.',[C('wary.s1','谨慎；提防','The hikers were wary of the unstable bridge and crossed one at a time.','健行者提防著不穩的橋，於是一次一人通過。','wary of + danger / person','Adjective: careful about danger or not quick to trust.','They proceed cautiously around a risk.'),C('wary.s2','警觉','The wary fox paused and listened before leaving its den.','警覺的狐狸在離開洞穴前停下來聆聽。','a wary animal / look','Adjective: watching closely and ready to avoid trouble.','The fox stays alert to danger.')],[M('The hikers were wary of the unstable bridge, so they ran across without looking or checking its condition.','The hikers were wary of the unstable bridge, so they checked it and crossed one at a time.','Wary people act cautiously rather than ignoring a known danger.')],[Q('wary.q1','wary.s1','meaning','Why did the hikers cross one at a time?','They were cautious about the unstable bridge.','They were celebrating a safe new bridge.','They were waiting for a court verdict.','Wary means careful about possible danger.'),Q('wary.q2','wary.s2','context','What did the fox do before leaving its den?','Paused and listened alertly.','Ran out without noticing anything.','Started singing a warble.','The animal sense means watchful and ready to avoid trouble.'),Q('wary.q3','wary.s1','distinction','Which person is wary of a stranger?','Someone cautious and slow to trust.','Someone who immediately accepts every claim.','Someone who issues a warranty.','Wary can describe caution about trust.'),Q('wary.q4','wary.s2','word-choice','Choose the alert-animal use.','A wary deer lifted its head at the faint sound.','The hikers were wary of the damaged bridge.','A wary employee refused a suspicious offer.','The first shows an animal watching closely.')]);
P('was able to','Past form of be able to; it says someone had the ability or opportunity to do something.',[C('was able to.s1','能够；可以','Despite the heavy snow, the rescue team was able to reach the cabin before dark.','儘管大雪紛飛，救援隊仍能在天黑前抵達小屋。','was able to + base verb','Phrase: used to say that someone had the ability or opportunity to do something.','The team succeeded in reaching the cabin.')],[M('The rescue team was able to reach the cabin, but it had no ability or opportunity to get there.','The rescue team was unable to reach the cabin because it lacked the ability or opportunity.','Was able to states that the action was possible or achieved.')],[Q('was able to.q1','was able to.s1','meaning','What did the rescue team manage to do?','Reach the cabin before dark.','Remain at the starting point.','Repair the weather.','Was able to describes an ability or successful opportunity.'),Q('was able to.q2','was able to.s1','context','Which sentence shows a successful past action?','After the bridge reopened, we were able to cross.','We were able to cross, but the bridge stayed closed and we did not cross.','We will be able to cross next year.','The first says the crossing became possible and occurred.'),Q('was able to.q3','was able to.s1','grammar','What form follows was able to?','A base verb, such as reach.','A noun only.','A past-tense verb such as reached.','The construction is was able to + verb base.'),Q('was able to.q4','was able to.s1','distinction','Which phrase best contrasts “was able to open it”?','could not open it','was able to opened it','was able opening it','Could not expresses lack of ability.')]);
P('wash','From Old English wascan, “clean with water”; it can mean cleanse, carry away by water, be washable or believable, or a washing.',[C('wash.s1','洗涤','Wash the berries under cold running water before serving them.','上桌前，請用冷水沖洗莓果。','wash clothes / hands / fruit','Verb: clean a person or thing with water, usually with soap.','The berries are cleaned with water.'),C('wash.s2','冲走','Heavy rain washed soil from the hillside and exposed the roots.','大雨沖走山坡上的土壤，露出了樹根。','wash away / off + material','Verb: carry something away through the movement of water.','Rainwater removes soil.'),C('wash.s3','耐洗；说得通','The blue dye washed well, and her explanation did not wash with the auditors.','藍色染料耐洗，而她的說法未能說服稽核員。','wash well; an excuse does not wash','Verb: be able to be cleaned without damage, or be believable.','The first clause concerns durability; the second, credibility.'),C('wash.s4','洗衣；洗涤物','I have a large wash to do before the guests arrive.','客人抵達前，我有一大批衣物要洗。','do / put on a wash','Noun: an act of cleaning with water or clothes waiting to be washed.','The phrase refers to laundry.')],[M('Heavy rain washed the soil uphill and covered the tree roots with more earth.','Heavy rain washed soil downhill and exposed the tree roots.','Water flowing down a hillside carries soil away rather than uphill.')],[Q('wash.q1','wash.s1','meaning','What should happen before the berries are served?','They should be cleaned under cold water.','They should be put in a wardrobe.','They should be covered with wallpaper.','Wash can mean clean with water.'),Q('wash.q2','wash.s2','context','What did heavy rain do to the hillside soil?','Carried it away and exposed roots.','Made it warmer.','Turned it into a warranty.','Water can wash material away.'),Q('wash.q3','wash.s3','distinction','What does “the dye washes well” mean?','It survives cleaning without damage or fading.','It is carried downhill by rain.','It is a pile of dirty laundry.','This use means the color is washable.'),Q('wash.q4','wash.s4','word-choice','Choose the laundry-noun use.','There is a wash waiting beside the machine.','Please wash the cups before dinner.','Floodwater washed away the soil.','The first names clothes waiting to be washed.')]);
P('washing','From wash + -ing; it names the activity of cleaning or a load of clothes waiting to be washed.',[C('washing.s1','洗涤活动','The washing of the laboratory glassware took place in a separate room.','實驗室玻璃器皿的清洗工作在另一個房間進行。','washing dishes / clothes','Noun: the activity of cleaning with water and soap or detergent.','The glassware is being cleaned.'),C('washing.s2','待洗衣物','A basket of washing stood beside the machine until the cycle finished.','洗衣機運轉結束前，一籃待洗衣物放在旁邊。','a load / basket of washing','Noun: clothes and sheets waiting to be washed.','The basket contains laundry.')],[M('The washing in the basket was already clean, dry, and put away, with no clothes left to be washed.','The washing in the basket still needed to be washed.','Washing as a load refers to clothes awaiting cleaning.')],[Q('washing.q1','washing.s1','meaning','What took place in the separate room?','Cleaning the laboratory glassware with water.','Storing clean uniforms in a wardrobe.','A courtroom hearing.','Washing can name the cleaning activity.'),Q('washing.q2','washing.s2','context','What was in the basket?','Clothes and sheets waiting for a wash.','Clean dishes ready to serve.','A dog waiting to be walked.','This sense names laundry waiting to be washed.'),Q('washing.q3','washing.s1','distinction','Which phrase names an activity?','The washing of dishes took twenty minutes.','A basket of washing stood nearby.','She put the washing in a hamper.','The first describes the act of cleaning.'),Q('washing.q4','washing.s2','word-choice','Choose the laundry-load use.','I folded the washing after the machine stopped.','Washing the windows took all morning.','They washed the windows carefully.','The first refers to clothes that were laundered.')]);
P('wasp','From Old English wæps; it names a stinging insect, often marked with yellow and black stripes.',[C('wasp.s1','黄蜂','A wasp circled the picnic table, so the children moved their juice cups indoors.','一隻黃蜂在野餐桌旁盤旋，孩子們便把果汁杯移到室內。','a wasp nest / sting','Noun: a large insect, often yellow and black, that can sting.','The insect approaches the food and can sting.')],[M('The wasp was a harmless mammal with fur and flippers that could not sting.','The walrus was a mammal with flippers; the wasp was a stinging insect.','A wasp is an insect capable of stinging, not a mammal.')],[Q('wasp.q1','wasp.s1','meaning','Why did the children move their drinks?','A stinging insect circled the table.','A walrus approached the picnic.','The table had a loose waistline.','A wasp is an insect that can sting.'),Q('wasp.q2','wasp.s1','context','Where might people find a wasp nest?','Hanging from a sheltered eave or branch.','Inside a railway waiting room.','In a wallet.','Wasps build nests and can sting.'),Q('wasp.q3','wasp.s1','distinction','Which description fits a wasp?','A yellow-and-black insect with a sting.','A large Arctic sea mammal.','A bird known for warbling.','The first describes a common wasp.'),Q('wasp.q4','wasp.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','A wasp flew near the fruit and everyone stepped back.','A wasp hauled itself onto sea ice.','A wasp sang from a willow branch.','The first is an insect approaching food.')]);
P('wastage','From waste + -age; it means loss caused by inefficient use, leakage, or people leaving.',[C('wastage.s1','浪费量','The factory reduced water wastage by repairing leaks in its pipes.','工廠修好管線漏水後，減少了用水浪費。','reduce / prevent / measure wastage','Noun: loss caused by use, leakage, or people leaving.','Repairing leaks reduces lost water.')],[M('The factory reduced water wastage by opening more leaks and letting clean water drain away.','The factory increased water wastage by opening more leaks.','More leakage increases, rather than reduces, wastage.')],[Q('wastage.q1','wastage.s1','meaning','How did the factory reduce water wastage?','It repaired leaking pipes.','It opened more leaks.','It added water to the wallpaper.','Wastage is loss caused by leakage or inefficient use.'),Q('wastage.q2','wastage.s1','context','What could staff turnover wastage mean?','Loss of trained employees who leave.','A new group of employees arriving.','A warning sign on a pipe.','The word can name loss when people leave.'),Q('wastage.q3','wastage.s1','distinction','Which action reduces material wastage?','Cutting fabric to a plan that uses nearly every piece.','Discarding usable fabric without checking it.','Leaving a tap leaking overnight.','Efficient use prevents loss.'),Q('wastage.q4','wastage.s1','word-choice','Choose the leakage-related use.','A broken valve caused water wastage overnight.','The city declared wartime.','The shop sold handmade wares.','The first names loss of water through leakage.')]);
P('waste','From Old North French waster, “spoil or devastate,” from Latin vastare, “lay waste”; meanings include misuse, physical decline, refuse, a futile act, and barrenness.',[C('waste.s1','浪费','Do not waste clean water while brushing your teeth.','刷牙時不要浪費乾淨的水。','waste time / money / resources','Verb: use more than needed or use something badly.','The water is used unnecessarily.'),C('waste.s2','消瘦；耗损','The untreated illness caused him to waste away over several months.','未治療的疾病使他在幾個月內逐漸消瘦衰弱。','waste away; a wasting illness','Verb: become thinner and weaker, or cause the body to do so.','The illness weakens his body.'),C('waste.s3','废弃物','The laboratory separates chemical waste from ordinary rubbish.','實驗室把化學廢棄物與一般垃圾分開。','industrial / chemical / household waste','Noun: unwanted material that is thrown away.','The chemicals are discarded material.'),C('waste.s4','白费','It would be a waste to print the report before checking its figures.','核對數字前就印出報告，將是白費功夫。','a waste of time / effort','Noun: an act of using something badly so that it brings no result.','Printing too early would not help.'),C('waste.s5','荒芜的','The abandoned mine left a waste landscape where few plants could grow.','廢棄礦場留下荒蕪景觀，幾乎沒有植物能生長。','a waste area / land','Adjective: unused, unproductive, or left empty.','The land is barren and unused.')],[M('The factory wasted water by using exactly the amount needed and preventing every leak.','The factory conserved water by using only what was needed and preventing leaks.','Using no more than necessary is conservation, not waste.')],[Q('waste.q1','waste.s1','meaning','What should people avoid while brushing?','Using more clean water than necessary.','Repairing a leaking pipe.','Separating chemical rubbish.','Waste as a verb can mean use resources badly.'),Q('waste.q2','waste.s2','context','What happened to him during the untreated illness?','He became thinner and weaker over time.','He gained strength quickly.','He stored goods in a warehouse.','Waste away means become physically weak and thin.'),Q('waste.q3','waste.s3','distinction','What did the laboratory separate?','Unwanted chemical material from ordinary rubbish.','A futile act from a useful one.','A barren field from a garden wall.','Waste as a noun can mean discarded material.'),Q('waste.q4','waste.s4','word-choice','Choose the futile-action sense.','It was a waste of effort to repeat a test that had no result.','The plant sent chemical waste for disposal.','The patient began to waste away.','The first describes effort bringing no useful result.')]);
P('wasteful','From waste + -ful; it can describe using too many resources or effort that produces no useful result.',[C('wasteful.s1','浪费的','Leaving every office light on overnight is wasteful.','整夜讓辦公室所有燈都亮著是很浪費的。','wasteful use / spending','Adjective: using more money, time, or resources than needed.','Electricity is consumed without need.'),C('wasteful.s2','徒劳无益的','The team stopped its wasteful search after confirming the missing file had been deleted permanently.','確認遺失檔案已永久刪除後，團隊停止了徒勞的搜尋。','a wasteful effort / exercise','Adjective: producing no useful result, so effort is wasted.','The search cannot recover the file.')],[M('Leaving every light on in an empty office all night was resource-saving and not wasteful.','Leaving every light on in an empty office all night was wasteful.','Unneeded electricity use consumes resources without benefit.')],[Q('wasteful.q1','wasteful.s1','meaning','Why is leaving all the lights on wasteful?','It uses electricity when no one needs it.','It saves every resource.','It prevents all power use.','Wasteful describes using more resources than needed.'),Q('wasteful.q2','wasteful.s2','context','Why did the team stop its search?','It could not produce a useful result because the file was deleted.','The search had already found the file.','The team wanted to use more effort.','A wasteful effort brings no useful outcome.'),Q('wasteful.q3','wasteful.s1','distinction','Which policy is wasteful?','Printing every draft when one reviewed copy would do.','Reusing paper for notes.','Turning off unused lights.','The first consumes more resources than necessary.'),Q('wasteful.q4','wasteful.s2','word-choice','Choose the futile-effort use.','Continuing the search after the only copy was destroyed was wasteful.','Buying excess supplies was wasteful.','Leaving the heating on in an empty room was wasteful.','The first describes effort that cannot succeed.')]);
P('wasteland','From waste + land; it names barren damaged terrain and, figuratively, a place lacking creativity, hope, or morality.',[C('wasteland.s1','荒地','The abandoned mine left a wasteland where little could grow.','廢棄礦場留下荒地，幾乎沒有植物能生長。','an industrial / barren wasteland','Noun: land that is barren, ruined, or unfit for growth.' ,'The ground has been damaged and cannot support plants.'),C('wasteland.s2','精神荒漠','The critic called the repetitive television schedule a cultural wasteland.','評論家稱重複的電視節目安排是文化荒漠。','a cultural / emotional wasteland','Noun: a place or situation lacking creativity, hope, or moral values.','The schedule offers little creative value.')],[M('The abandoned mine created a wasteland where fertile soil supported thriving gardens everywhere.','The abandoned mine created a wasteland where few plants could grow.','A wasteland is barren or ruined, not fertile and thriving.')],[Q('wasteland.q1','wasteland.s1','meaning','What did the abandoned mine leave behind?','Barren land where little could grow.','A fertile orchard.','A hospital ward.','A wasteland is ruined or unproductive terrain.'),Q('wasteland.q2','wasteland.s2','context','Why did the critic call the schedule a cultural wasteland?','It lacked creative value.','It was full of original and varied programs.','It had a garden with fertile soil.','The figurative sense describes a place lacking creativity.'),Q('wasteland.q3','wasteland.s1','distinction','Which is a literal wasteland?','A polluted field where crops no longer grow.','A lively arts center.','A well-watered orchard.','The first is barren or ruined land.'),Q('wasteland.q4','wasteland.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','The novelist described the town’s cultural wasteland.','The mine left a physical wasteland.','The farmer restored the wasteland soil.','The first describes an absence of cultural life.')]);
P('waster','From waste + -er; it names someone who squanders resources and can also name a defective rejected item.',[C('waster.s1','挥霍者','The office called him a waster because he discarded usable supplies without checking them.','辦公室稱他是揮霍者，因為他未經檢查就丟棄可用物資。','a time / money / resource waster','Noun: someone who squanders resources; also an item rejected as defective.','He discards things that could still be used.'),C('waster.s1','废品','The inspection line separated each defective waster from products ready for sale.','檢查線把每件有缺陷的廢品與可出售產品分開。','a defective / rejected waster','Noun: an article rejected because it is defective or unusable.','The damaged product is rejected.')],[M('The waster saved every usable supply and never discarded or misused anything.','The careful employee saved every usable supply and never wasted anything.','A person who saves and uses resources carefully is not a waster.')],[Q('waster.q1','waster.s1','meaning','Why did the office call him a waster?','He discarded usable supplies carelessly.','He repaired all damaged products.','He issued a search warrant.','A waster can be someone who squanders resources.'),Q('waster.q2','waster.s1','context','What happened to the defective item on the line?','It was separated as a rejected waster.','It was sold as a perfect product.','It was placed in a waiting room.','Waster can also mean an item rejected as defective.'),Q('waster.q3','waster.s1','distinction','Which person is a waster?','Someone who repeatedly throws away usable food.','Someone who saves materials for reuse.','Someone who checks product quality.','The first squanders resources.'),Q('waster.q4','waster.s1','word-choice','Choose the defective-item use.','The cracked tile was marked as a waster.','The worker was a waster of company time.','The waster threw away the supplies.','The first uses waster for a rejected article.')]);
P('wastewater','A compound of waste + water; it is used water from homes, farms, or factories that carries waste.',[C('wastewater.s1','废水','The plant filters wastewater from the dyeing process before releasing it.','工廠在排放前先過濾染色製程產生的廢水。','treat / filter / discharge wastewater','Noun: used water from homes, farms, or factories carrying waste.' ,'The factory treats water after use.')],[M('The factory released wastewater directly into the stream after removing every contaminant and making it clean drinking water.','The factory treated its wastewater before releasing it into the stream.','Untreated wastewater has not been made clean drinking water.')],[Q('wastewater.q1','wastewater.s1','meaning','What did the plant filter?','Used water from its dyeing process.','A clean water supply before use.','A batch of laundry.','Wastewater is used water carrying waste.'),Q('wastewater.q2','wastewater.s1','context','Which source can produce wastewater?','A household drain after washing dishes.','A sealed bottle of untouched spring water.','A dry paper wall covering.','Used household water can become wastewater.'),Q('wastewater.q3','wastewater.s1','distinction','Why should a factory treat wastewater?','It may carry waste before being released.','It is already guaranteed to be drinking water.','It is a kind of dry refuse.','Treatment removes or reduces contaminants.'),Q('wastewater.q4','wastewater.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','The farm reused treated wastewater to irrigate trees.','The farm stored clean unused water as wastewater.','The farm called its warranty wastewater.','The first refers to used water that has been treated.')]);
P('watch','From Old English wæccan, “keep awake or be vigilant”; it can mean observe, be careful, guard, a timepiece, or a period of duty.',[C('watch.s1','观看','We watched the eclipse through protective glasses from the school field.','我們在學校操場戴著防護眼鏡觀看日食。','watch a match / show / event','Verb: look at someone or something for a period of time.','They observe the eclipse.'),C('watch.s2','当心','Watch the step at the entrance; the stone is uneven.','小心入口處的台階；石面不平。','watch + noun; watch out for','Verb: be careful or pay attention to prevent trouble.','The speaker warns someone about a hazard.'),C('watch.s3','看管','Could you watch the children while I speak to the teacher?','我和老師談話時，你能幫忙照看孩子們嗎？','watch over / watch someone','Verb: stay with someone or something to guard or care for it.','The person supervises the children.'),C('watch.s4','手表','His watch stopped at noon, so he reset it beside the station clock.','他的手錶在中午停了，因此他在車站時鐘旁重新校時。','a wristwatch / watch face','Noun: a small clock worn or carried by a person.','The object displays time.'),C('watch.s5','值班','The night watch ended when the next guard arrived at six.','早上六點下一位警衛抵達時，夜間值班結束。','stand / keep a watch','Noun: a period of time spent guarding, or the person doing it.','The phrase names a guard’s duty period.')],[M('She watched the eclipse by turning away from it and refusing to look at the sky.','She missed the eclipse because she turned away and did not watch it.','To watch an event is to look at it.')],[Q('watch.q1','watch.s1','meaning','What did the class observe through protective glasses?','The eclipse.','A wristwatch repair.','A night guard’s shift.','Watch as a verb can mean observe an event.'),Q('watch.q2','watch.s2','context','What should visitors do at the uneven step?','Be careful.','Look at a television show.','Guard a building overnight.','Watch can warn someone to pay attention.'),Q('watch.q3','watch.s4','distinction','What stopped at noon?','A small timepiece the man wore.','The eclipse.','The night guard’s duty.','Watch as a noun can mean a small clock.'),Q('watch.q4','watch.s5','word-choice','Choose the guard-duty use.','The second watch began after midnight.','She watched the film twice.','He repaired his watch.','The first names a period spent guarding.')]);
P('watch out','From watch + out; an imperative phrasal verb telling someone to be careful about a possible danger.',[C('watch out.s1','小心；当心','Watch out for the loose cable before you carry the ladder past it.','把梯子搬過去前，小心那條鬆脫的電纜。','watch out for + danger / obstacle','Phrasal verb: be careful because a danger or problem may be present.','The speaker warns about an obstacle.')],[M('“Watch out!” the guide shouted as the hiker stepped toward the open shaft, meaning the route was perfectly safe.','“Watch out!” the guide shouted as the hiker approached the dangerous shaft.','Watch out is a warning to be careful, not reassurance that there is no danger.')],[Q('watch out.q1','watch out.s1','meaning','Why did the guide shout “Watch out”?','The hiker was approaching an open shaft.','The hiker had finished a safe tour.','The guide wanted the hiker to look at a film.','Watch out warns of a nearby danger.'),Q('watch out.q2','watch out.s1','context','What does “watch out for falling rocks” mean?','Be alert because rocks may fall.','Study the rocks after they have been removed.','Watch a documentary about geology.','Watch out for introduces a possible hazard.'),Q('watch out.q3','watch out.s1','distinction','Which instruction is a warning?','Watch out for the wet floor.','Watch the clock for five minutes.','Watch over the sleeping child.','The first warns someone to avoid danger.'),Q('watch out.q4','watch out.s1','grammar','What commonly follows watch out in a hazard warning?','for + a danger or problem','at + a person only','of + a past-tense verb','The pattern is watch out for something.')]);
P('watchdog','From watch + dog; it can name a dog that guards property or an organization monitoring power and misconduct.',[C('watchdog.s1','看门狗；监察机构','An independent watchdog investigated complaints about the company’s data practices.','一個獨立監察機構調查了對該公司資料處理方式的投訴。','a consumer / government watchdog','Noun: a guardian dog or an organization that monitors government or business.','The organization checks a company’s conduct.')],[M('The consumer watchdog protected the company from scrutiny by hiding every complaint and refusing to investigate.','The consumer watchdog investigated complaints and monitored the company.','A watchdog monitors conduct; concealing all complaints fails that role.')],[Q('watchdog.q1','watchdog.s1','meaning','What did the independent watchdog investigate?','Complaints about the company’s data practices.','A worker’s weekly wage.','A damaged railway wagon.','A watchdog can be an organization monitoring business.'),Q('watchdog.q2','watchdog.s1','context','Which group could be a government watchdog?','An independent group checking public officials’ conduct.','A group that sells dog food.','A group that guards a private garden only.','The figurative watchdog monitors government.'),Q('watchdog.q3','watchdog.s1','distinction','What does a guard dog watchdog do literally?','Guards property and alerts people to intruders.','Checks whether a law is fair.','Keeps time on a person’s wrist.','The literal sense is a dog that guards.'),Q('watchdog.q4','watchdog.s1','word-choice','Choose the oversight use.','A watchdog agency audited public spending.','A watchdog barked at the gate.','The watch ended at dawn.','The agency monitors government activity.')]);
P('watcher','From watch + -er; it means a person who observes, keeps guard, or watches as a hobby or duty.',[C('watcher.s1','守望者；观察者','A bird watcher recorded the heron’s arrival without disturbing the nest.','一名觀鳥者記錄了蒼鷺到來的時間，沒有打擾鳥巢。','a bird / star / close watcher','Noun: someone who looks on, observes, or keeps guard as a duty or hobby.','The person observes birds carefully.')],[M('The bird watcher recorded the heron without looking at it, observing it, or keeping any watch.','The bird watcher recorded the heron while observing it from a distance.','A watcher observes what is happening.')],[Q('watcher.q1','watcher.s1','meaning','What did the bird watcher record?','The heron’s arrival.','The factory’s weekly wages.','A legal search warrant.','A watcher observes and records what happens.'),Q('watcher.q2','watcher.s1','context','Who is a star watcher?','Someone who observes stars as a hobby.','Someone who repairs wristwatches.','Someone who fights in wartime.','A watcher can observe as a hobby.'),Q('watcher.q3','watcher.s1','distinction','What does a watcher do at a night post?','Keeps guard and observes the area.','Changes the building’s wallpaper.','Carries a water supply.','A watcher may observe as a duty.'),Q('watcher.q4','watcher.s1','word-choice','Choose the observer sense.','A watcher noticed the lights go out across the harbor.','The night watch lasted until dawn.','The guard watched over the child.','The first names a person who observes.')]);
P('watchful','From watch + -ful; it describes alert attention to danger or close attention to someone’s actions.',[C('watchful.s1','警觉的','The watchful deer lifted its head whenever a branch snapped nearby.','附近樹枝每次折斷時，警覺的鹿都會抬起頭。','a watchful guard / animal','Adjective: carefully noticing everything because danger or change may come.','The deer listens for possible danger.'),C('watchful.s2','密切注意','The editor kept a watchful eye on the figures as the final report was assembled.','編輯在整理最終報告時，密切留意各項數字。','keep a watchful eye on','Adjective: attending closely to what someone or something is doing.','The editor monitors the figures closely.')],[M('The watchful guard ignored every alarm, looked away from the gate, and noticed no movement.','The inattentive guard ignored alarms and failed to notice movement.','A watchful person pays close attention rather than ignoring signals.')],[Q('watchful.q1','watchful.s1','meaning','How did the deer react to a nearby snap?','It lifted its head alertly.','It continued sleeping without noticing.','It wandered into a waiting room.','Watchful means alert to danger or change.'),Q('watchful.q2','watchful.s2','context','What did the editor keep an eye on?','The figures in the report.','A dog’s walking route.','A wristwatch’s battery.','This sense means paying close attention to an activity.'),Q('watchful.q3','watchful.s1','distinction','Which guard is watchful?','One who notices a faint sound and checks the gate.','One who sleeps through every alarm.','One who leaves the gate unattended.','The first remains alert.'),Q('watchful.q4','watchful.s2','word-choice','Choose the close-monitoring use.','The nurse kept a watchful eye on the patient’s breathing.','The watchful owl scanned the dark field.','A watchful guard listened for intruders.','The first describes close attention to a person’s condition.')]);
P('watchman','From watch + man; it names a person employed to guard a building, especially at night, or anyone standing watch.',[C('watchman.s1','看守；巡夜人','The watchman made a round of the warehouse before locking the outer gate.','看守人在鎖上外門前巡視了倉庫一圈。','a night / security watchman','Noun: a person employed to guard a building or grounds, usually at night.','He checks the premises as part of his job.'),C('watchman.s2','值守者','A watchman stood at the bridge entrance and kept unauthorized visitors from crossing.','一名守衛站在橋入口，阻止未獲許可的訪客通過。','stand watch; a watchman on duty','Noun: anyone who stands watch and controls entry or exit.','The person guards the entrance.')],[M('The watchman guarded the warehouse by leaving the gates open and allowing every stranger to enter.','The watchman secured the warehouse by checking the gates and challenging strangers.','A watchman guards a site rather than leaving it open to intruders.')],[Q('watchman.q1','watchman.s1','meaning','What did the watchman do before locking the gate?','Patrolled the warehouse.','Prepared the evening meal.','Issued a search warrant.','A watchman is employed to guard a building.'),Q('watchman.q2','watchman.s2','context','What did the person at the bridge entrance do?','Prevented unauthorized visitors from crossing.','Sold the bridge as a product.','Waited for a bus without watching.','This sense is anyone standing guard at an entrance.'),Q('watchman.q3','watchman.s1','distinction','Which job is a watchman’s?','Patrolling a site at night to protect it.','Monitoring a company’s data as an agency.','Observing birds as a hobby.','The first is a paid guard role.'),Q('watchman.q4','watchman.s2','word-choice','Choose the gatekeeping use.','A watchman checked passes at the stadium entrance.','The watchman completed a night patrol around the warehouse.','A wristwatch stopped at noon.','The first focuses on controlling entry.')]);
P('watchword','From watch + word; it can be a sentry’s password or a phrase expressing a group’s guiding aim.',[C('watchword.s1','口令；暗语','The sentry asked each visitor for the watchword before opening the camp gate.','哨兵在打開營地大門前，要求每位訪客說出口令。','give / know / change the watchword','Noun: a word or phrase used by guards to distinguish friends from strangers.','The password confirms identity.'),C('watchword.s2','口号；格言','“Measure twice, cut once” became the workshop’s watchword for careful work.','「量兩次，切一次」成了工坊謹慎工作的格言。','a watchword for + value / group','Noun: a word or phrase expressing a group’s aims or guiding principle.','The saying sums up the workshop’s rule.')],[M('The sentry opened the gate to every stranger without asking for the watchword or checking identity.','The sentry checked each visitor’s identity by asking for the watchword.','A watchword serves as a password for distinguishing friends from strangers.')],[Q('watchword.q1','watchword.s1','meaning','What did the sentry request at the gate?','A password to confirm the visitor’s identity.','A weekly wage receipt.','A product warranty.','A watchword can be a guard’s password.'),Q('watchword.q2','watchword.s2','context','What did the workshop’s phrase express?','Its principle of checking measurements carefully.','The camp’s entry password.','A watchman’s patrol schedule.','This sense is a guiding phrase or motto.'),Q('watchword.q3','watchword.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses watchword as a password?','The guards changed the watchword at midnight.','“Safety first” was the team’s watchword.','The word appeared in a poem.','The first refers to a password used by guards.'),Q('watchword.q4','watchword.s2','word-choice','Choose the motto use.','Fairness became the committee’s watchword.','The sentry demanded the watchword before entry.','The watchman checked the password at the gate.','The first expresses a group’s guiding aim.')]);
})();
